## SUMMARY

<span lang="ja">SimpleModelingとTextusは、Literate Model-Driven Cloud-Native Development with Object-Functional Paradigms for the AI Eraをテーマに、開発方法論と実行環境を一体化した技術体系です。文芸モデル駆動開発、オブジェクト・関数統合、コンポーネント指向、クラウド・ネイティブ技術を組み合わせ、AI時代のクラウド・ネイティブな業務アプリケーションのための開発方法論とアプリケーション・フレームワークを提供します。</span><span lang="en">SimpleModeling and Textus form an integrated technology system combining a development methodology with an execution environment under the theme “Literate Model-Driven Cloud-Native Development with Object-Functional Paradigms for the AI Era.” They combine literate model-driven development, object-functional paradigms, component orientation, and cloud-native technologies, providing a development methodology and application framework for cloud-native business applications in the AI era.</span>

<span lang="ja">本書は、CBDによるコンポーネントの独立性と、認証・認可などの共通機構を組み合わせるセキュリティ・アーキテクチャを解説します。別技術で構築するPresentation tierを信頼の前提にせず、Application・Domainの役割分担とDomain内部の対策で保護する構成を示します。モデルに記述した規則を、検査・配布・受入れから実行・観測・復旧へ引き継ぐ流れも説明します。</span><span lang="en">This guide explains a security architecture that combines component independence through CBD with shared mechanisms such as authentication and authorization. It describes protection through Application and Domain responsibilities and controls within the Domain, without assuming trust in a Presentation tier built with other technologies. It also follows modeled rules through inspection, distribution, admission, execution, observation, and recovery.</span>

<span lang="ja">CMLでモデルを定義し、Textusの標準構成で実行・運用することで、一般的な認証・認可の機構が自動的に適用されます。開発者は機構そのものを部品ごとに実装せず、利用する認証方式と業務固有の権限をモデル・設定で指定します。通常の開発と運用を通して基本的な保護を得ながら、用途に応じて認可を細かく調整できます。</span><span lang="en">Defining models in CML and running them with the standard Textus configuration automatically applies common authentication and authorization mechanisms. Developers specify the authentication method and business-specific permissions through models and configuration rather than implementing these mechanisms in each component. Ordinary development and operation provide baseline protection, with authorization refined for each application.</span>

# Introducing SimpleModeling and Textus｜SimpleModelingとTextusの全体像

<span lang="ja">SimpleModelingは開発の方法論と作法を、Textusはアプリケーションの実行・運用基盤を提供します。</span><span lang="en">SimpleModeling provides the development methodology and conventions; Textus provides the application execution and operational platform.</span>

<span lang="ja">CMLで業務モデルを記述し、Cozyで生成する実装やコンポーネントをTextusへ接続します。以下では、セキュリティの適用経路を理解するために必要な全体構成を示します。</span><span lang="en">Business models are written in CML, and implementations and components generated by Cozy are connected to Textus. The following overview establishes the architecture needed to understand how security controls are applied.</span>

<span lang="ja">セキュリティは、この開発・実行・運用を通じて扱う設計上の主題です。</span><span lang="en">Security is an architectural concern spanning this development, execution, and operation.</span>

## The SimpleModeling Technology System｜SimpleModelingの技術体系

<span lang="ja">SimpleModelingは、文芸モデル駆動開発を軸に、業務知識からソフトウェアの開発・実行・運用までをつなぐ方法論と技術体系です。文芸モデルでは、業務の背景、目的、要求、判断理由を文章と構造化したモデルで表します。用語集とBoK（知識体系）を通して文書とモデルの意味を対応付け、人間と生成AIが開発の文脈を共有できるようにします。</span><span lang="en">SimpleModeling is a methodology and technology system centered on literate model-driven development, connecting business knowledge to software development, execution, and operation. Literate models express business context, goals, requirements, and rationale through prose and structured models. Glossaries and a Body of Knowledge (BoK) relate the meaning of documents and models so that people and generative AI can share development context.</span>

<span lang="ja">この体系は、ドメイン・モデリング、モデル駆動、オブジェクト・関数統合型プログラミング、コンポーネント指向開発、クラウド・ネイティブ・アプリケーション構築を組み合わせています。ドメイン・モデリングは業務の概念と規則を捉え、モデル駆動はそれを実装と実行へつなぎます。オブジェクトと関数の統合は状態と計算の表現を支え、コンポーネント指向は契約を持つ部品の組合せを、クラウド・ネイティブは実行環境への配備と継続的な運用を支えます。</span><span lang="en">The system combines domain modeling, model-driven development, object-functional programming, component-based development, and cloud-native application development. Domain modeling captures business concepts and rules, while model-driven development connects them to implementation and execution. Object-functional programming supports the expression of state and computation, components compose parts through contracts, and cloud-native techniques support deployment and ongoing operation.</span>

<span lang="ja">知識処理では、文芸モデル、ドメインのモデル、開発に用いる知識を用語によって結び付けます。SimpleModeling.orgが提供する技術情報とBoKを基礎に、プロジェクト固有の用語、ドメイン知識、設計上の判断を加えます。これらを人間が読む文書として利用するとともに、生成AIが参照する外部知識へ接続することで、モデルの記述・レビュー・生成を支える構成を目指します。</span><span lang="en">Knowledge processing connects literate models, domain models, and development knowledge through shared terms. Technical material and the BoK provided by SimpleModeling.org form a foundation to which projects add terminology, domain knowledge, and design decisions. The aim is to use this information both as human-readable documentation and as external knowledge for generative AI, supporting model authoring, review, and generation.</span>

## Connect CML Models to Generation and Direct Execution｜CMLのモデルを生成と直接実行へつなぐ

<span lang="ja">CMLで業務の構造、振る舞い、制約を記述し、実行可能なモデルはTextusが直接解釈・実行します。Cozyは型付きAPIや実装の接続構造、コンポーネントの構成を生成します。モデルの直接実行とコード生成を組み合わせ、個別の補完処理を標準の実行経路へ接続します。</span><span lang="en">CML describes business structures, behavior, and constraints, and Textus directly interprets and executes executable models. Cozy generates typed APIs, implementation connections, and component structures. Direct model execution and code generation connect application-specific supplementary processing to standard execution paths.</span>

<span lang="ja">モデルで定めた操作・状態・制約を実行へ引き継ぐことで、業務の概念を実装ごとに書き直す箇所を減らします。補完実装にも同じ契約と権限の境界を適用します。</span><span lang="en">Carrying modeled operations, state, and constraints into execution reduces repeated manual translations of business concepts. Supplementary implementations follow the same contracts and authority boundaries.</span>

<span lang="ja">セキュリティの観点では、入力制約や操作の公開範囲、必要な権限がモデル上の説明に留まらず、生成物と実行時の判定へ引き継がれることが重要です。モデルの検査、生成された契約の確認、Textus上での認可と資源制御をつなぐことで、モデル駆動を保護の適用経路として利用します。</span><span lang="en">For security, input constraints, operation exposure, and required authority must be carried into generated artifacts and runtime decisions. Connecting model inspection and generated-contract checks to authorization and resource controls on Textus makes model-driven development a path for applying protection.</span>

## Textus and SAR/CAR｜TextusとSAR/CAR

<span lang="ja">Textusは、SimpleModelingで開発するアプリケーションとコンポーネントの実行・運用基盤です。業務処理の呼出し、データの管理、外部サービスとの連携、実行資源の管理、観測と運用などの共通機能を提供する体系として構成します。CNCF（Cloud-Native Component Framework）は、その中でコンポーネントの実行とクラウド環境への接続を支えるフレームワークです。</span><span lang="en">Textus is the execution and operational platform for applications and components developed with SimpleModeling. It is organized as shared infrastructure for business-operation invocation, data management, external-service integration, execution resources, observation, and operations. CNCF (Cloud-Native Component Framework) supports component execution and connection to cloud environments within that platform.</span>

<span lang="ja">SAR/CARは、アプリケーションやコンポーネントを構成・配布・利用するための単位として扱います。本書では特に、CARが持つ契約、依存関係、必要権限、実装を検査し、その内容を配備と実行へ対応付ける仕組みを説明します。開発者は業務固有の処理をこれらの単位へまとめ、Textusの共通機能と組み合わせます。</span><span lang="en">SARs and CARs are units for composing, distributing, and consuming applications and components. This guide focuses particularly on inspecting a CAR's contracts, dependencies, required authority, and implementation, and relating those contents to deployment and execution. Developers package application-specific behavior into these units and combine it with shared Textus facilities.</span>

<span lang="ja">業務処理が通る標準の呼出し・データアクセス・資源利用の経路へ、認証・認可、入力や出力の保護、資源制限、監査・観測を組み込みます。CMLの定義と基本設定をこれらの経路へ接続し、処理ごとに保護機構を実装する負担を減らします。</span><span lang="en">Authentication, authorization, input/output protection, resource limits, auditing, and observation are integrated into standard invocation, data-access, and resource-use paths. CML definitions and basic configuration connect to these paths, reducing per-handler security implementation.</span>

## Connecting Knowledge, Models, Generation, Execution, and Operations｜知識・モデル・生成・実行・運用をつなぐ全体アーキテクチャ

<span lang="ja">全体アーキテクチャの起点には、業務の要求や判断理由を表す文芸モデルと、用語集・BoKがあります。ドメイン・モデリングによって業務の構造と振る舞いを整理し、CMLで実行へつながるモデルを記述します。文書、用語、モデルの対応を保つことで、何を実現するのかと、なぜその規則が必要なのかを共有します。</span><span lang="en">The architecture starts with literate models of requirements and rationale, together with glossaries and the BoK. Domain modeling organizes business structure and behavior, and CML expresses models that lead to execution. Maintaining correspondence among documents, terms, and models shares both what must be implemented and why particular rules are required.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/architecture-security-map-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/architecture-security-map-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">知識から実行・運用までの各段階で、何を引き継ぎ、どの保護を担当するかを示します。</span><span lang="en">Each stage carries specific information forward and contributes protection, from knowledge through execution and operations.</span>

<span lang="ja">CozyはCMLのモデルを実装とコンポーネントへ変換し、SAR/CARとして構成する経路を支えます。生成した成果物は検査と配備時の受入れを経て、Textusの実行基盤で利用します。モデルの契約を生成物へ引き継ぐ部分と、その契約を実行時に適用する部分を、この接続によって一体にします。</span><span lang="en">Cozy transforms CML models into implementations and components and supports their composition as SAR/CAR artifacts. Generated artifacts undergo assessment and deployment admission before use on Textus. This connection joins the transfer of model contracts into artifacts with the runtime application of those contracts.</span>

<span lang="ja">実行・配備では、Presentation（UI）、Application、Domainの責務を分けます。Presentationは別技術で構築でき、Applicationが外部要求の受付と業務操作の組合せを、Domainが業務規則と状態の管理を担当します。運用では実行結果と資源利用を観測し、権限の見直し、修正、再配備へ戻します。</span><span lang="en">Execution and deployment separate Presentation (UI), Application, and Domain responsibilities. The Presentation tier may use other technologies; the Application tier receives external requests and coordinates business operations, while the Domain manages business rules and state. Operations observe results and resource use and feed them back into authority review, fixes, and redeployment.</span>

## Security Within the Overall Architecture｜全体アーキテクチャに組み込むセキュリティ

<span lang="ja">モデルは保護する対象と条件を記述し、CBDは規則を適用する接点を限定します。共通基盤がその接点で判定することで、個々の実装へ対策を繰り返し組み込む負担を減らします。</span><span lang="en">Models describe protected targets and conditions, and CBD limits the interfaces where rules apply. Shared infrastructure evaluates them at those interfaces, reducing repeated integration of controls into individual implementations.</span>

<span lang="ja">コンポーネントの独立性を保ちながら、Textus側の認証・認可の機構を共用します。一方、Presentation tierは別技術でも構築できるため、Textusの機構を直接利用することを前提にせず、サーバーとの境界で要求を検証します。</span><span lang="en">Components retain their independence while sharing authentication and authorization mechanisms on the Textus side. The Presentation tier may use other technologies, so direct use of Textus mechanisms is not assumed; requests are verified at the server boundary.</span>

<span lang="ja">次章では保護範囲と開発者・基盤の分担を定め、その後にモデル、検査、配布、実行、運用の接続を説明します。</span><span lang="en">The next chapter defines coverage and the division of responsibility between developers and the platform, followed by the connections among models, inspection, distribution, execution, and operations.</span>

# Build on Standard Protection for Application-Specific Security｜標準の保護から用途別の強化へ進む

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFは、通常の業務アプリケーションに必要な主要なセキュリティ機構を共通基盤に備えます。CMLで定義し、標準経路で実行・運用することで基本的な保護が適用されます。デフォルトは導入と日常運用のしやすさを重視し、特に初学者が個々の機構を組み立てる負担を減らします。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF provides the main security mechanisms needed by ordinary business applications through shared infrastructure. CML definitions and standard execution and operation paths apply baseline protection. Defaults prioritize ease of adoption and daily operation, especially reducing the burden on beginners of assembling individual mechanisms.</span>

<span lang="ja">この基本構成に、業務固有の認可規則と、必要に応じた機能制限・区画分離・復旧構成を組み合わせます。本書では各機構の役割と接続を説明し、最後に、用途別の構成を選びやすくする運用パターン・プロファイル・手順書の整備方針を示します。</span><span lang="en">Business-specific authorization rules and, where needed, capability restrictions, compartment isolation, and recovery arrangements build on this baseline. The guide explains the roles and connections of these mechanisms, then presents the planned patterns, profiles, and guides for selecting application-appropriate configurations.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/standard-to-hardened-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/standard-to-hardened-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">標準の保護を起点に、業務の認可と配備・運用上の強化を組み合わせます。下段は選択と設定を支える今後の整備方針です。</span><span lang="en">Standard protection combines with business authorization and deployment/operational hardening. The lower layer shows planned guidance for selection and configuration.</span>

## Cover Business-Application Protection from Development to Operation｜業務アプリケーションの保護を開発から運用まで揃える

<span lang="ja">保護の範囲は、認証、操作とデータの認可、入力・出力の保護、実行資源の制限、配布物の信頼性、監査・観測・復旧です。「フルセット」は、この一連の範囲を体系的に揃える設計を指します。標準経路で適用する機構、用途に応じて選ぶ構成、今後整備する項目を、各節で区別します。</span><span lang="en">Protection covers authentication, operation and data authorization, input/output handling, runtime resource limits, artifact trust, auditing, observation, and recovery. A full set refers to systematic coverage of this lifecycle. Each section distinguishes mechanisms applied through standard paths, configurations selected for particular uses, and planned additions.</span>

<span lang="ja">例えば、注文の更新要求では、利用者を認証するだけでなく、更新操作の利用権限、対象注文へのアクセス権限、入力制約、業務状態の変更条件を確認する必要があります。配備する実装の検査と実行資源の制限は、その処理を支える別の保護です。異常が発生した場合は、どの主体がどの注文を変更したかを追跡し、必要な権限失効と復旧へつなぎます。この一連の対応を共通基盤で支えることが、フルセットという目標の具体的な意味です。</span><span lang="en">For an order update, identifying the user is only one requirement. Permission to invoke the update, access to the target order, input constraints, and conditions for changing business state must also be checked. Inspection of the deployed implementation and resource limits provide additional protection. If an anomaly occurs, observations must connect the actor and order change to revocation and recovery. Supporting that complete path through shared infrastructure makes the full-set goal concrete.</span>

<span lang="ja">各機構の設計を理解するには、何を保護するか、どの境界で適用するか、誰が規則を定義するか、他の機構へ何を引き継ぐかを確認する必要があります。本書ではこの水準まで技術的に説明します。プロトコルの細部、APIの全仕様、設定項目の一覧、実装アルゴリズムは個別の技術記事と仕様書へ展開します。</span><span lang="en">Understanding each mechanism requires identifying what it protects, where it is enforced, who defines its rules, and what it passes to other mechanisms. This guide explains the architecture at that technical depth. Protocol details, complete API specifications, configuration catalogs, and implementation algorithms are developed in dedicated technical articles and specifications.</span>

## The Developer's Declarations and the Platform's Responsibilities｜開発者が記述することと基盤が担当すること

<span lang="ja">開発者はCMLで業務の構造・操作・状態変更を定義し、利用する認証方式や業務上の公開範囲を設定します。基本的な権限には既定値を利用し、用途固有の役割・関係・条件が必要な箇所を追加します。基盤が判定機構を提供し、モデルと設定が業務ごとの方針を表す分担です。</span><span lang="en">Developers define business structures, operations, and state changes in CML and configure authentication methods and business visibility. Defaults supply basic permissions, with application-specific roles, relationships, and conditions added where required. The platform supplies decision mechanisms, while models and configuration express business policy.</span>

<span lang="ja">CMLのOperationとEntityを標準経路で動かすと、認証された主体の受渡し、操作・対象データの認可、監査の記録が共通機構で働きます。開発者が業務処理ごとにこれらの呼出しを組み込む必要はありません。対象EntityのUNIX型権限と、その上に組み合わせる認可手法は、認証・認可の章で説明します。</span><span lang="en">Running CML Operations and Entities through standard paths invokes shared mechanisms for authenticated-subject propagation, operation and target-data authorization, and audit recording. Developers do not need to add these calls to each business handler. The authentication and authorization chapter explains UNIX-style target-Entity permissions and the authorization methods combined with them.</span>

<span lang="ja">例えば、特定部門の担当者に、処理中の注文だけを更新させる場合は、部門・担当関係・注文の状態を規則として指定します。共通基盤は、その規則を操作と対象データの判定点へ適用します。</span><span lang="en">For example, allowing a department’s assigned staff to update only in-progress orders requires rules for department, assignment, and order state. Shared infrastructure applies these rules at operation and target-data checkpoints.</span>

## Security as a First-Class Architectural Concern｜アーキテクチャの第一級要素としてのセキュリティ

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFでは、セキュリティをアプリケーション実装の後から追加する機能として扱いません。セキュリティは、システムの構造、権限、信頼境界、実行境界、配布単位、運用方式を決めるアーキテクチャ段階からの第一級要素です。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF treats security as a first-class concern at the architectural stage, when system structure, authority, trust boundaries, execution boundaries, distribution units, and operational practices are determined. It does not treat security as a feature to be added after application implementation.</span>

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFは、悪意ある攻撃、ソフトウェアの欠陥、運用ミス、AIによる誤判断を異なる原因として区別しつつ、それらが同じauthority boundaryを越えようとする問題として統一的に扱います。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF distinguishes malicious attacks, software defects, operational mistakes, and AI misjudgments as different causes, while addressing them through a common architectural concern: attempts to cross an authority boundary.</span>

<span lang="ja">ここでいう境界は、どの主体が、どの操作と資源を、どの条件で利用できるかを定めるものです。攻撃と誤操作の原因を同一視せず、許可されていない作用を制限する仕組みを共通化します。</span><span lang="en">A boundary defines which actors may use which operations and resources under which conditions. Attacks and mistakes remain distinct causes, while mechanisms restricting unauthorized effects can be shared.</span>

# How SimpleModeling Conventions Lead to Protection｜SimpleModelingの作法が保護の適用につながる仕組み

<span lang="ja">CBDで定めた責務と接点に、モデルで記述した操作・入力・状態・必要権限を対応付けます。これらをSAR/CARへ反映することで、部品の独立性と保護の条件を同じ対象について確認できます。</span><span lang="en">Operations, inputs, states, and required authority described in models are mapped to the responsibilities and interfaces defined by CBD. Reflecting them in SARs and CARs lets component independence and protection conditions be checked against the same artifact.</span>

<span lang="ja">共通の生成規則と検査を使い、モデルと実装の対応を確認します。検査結果は対象CARの版と内容に結び付け、次章の配布・受入れへ渡します。</span><span lang="en">Shared generation rules and checks verify correspondence between models and implementations. Inspection results are associated with a CAR’s version and content and passed into distribution and admission in the next chapter.</span>

<span lang="ja">開発者が記述する業務モデルと部品の契約を、共通基盤が適用できる保護の条件へつなぐことが、この開発経路の役割です。</span><span lang="en">This development path connects the business models and component contracts authored by developers to protection conditions that shared infrastructure can apply.</span>

## Security Supported by Component-Based Development｜コンポーネント指向開発が支えるセキュリティ

<span lang="ja">コンポーネント指向開発（CBD）は、SimpleModelingの根幹をなす開発方式です。責務の分離、部品の再利用と組合せ、変更の局所化、独立した検査や交換など、ソフトウェアの開発と運用に幅広い利点をもたらします。セキュリティも、こうしたCBDの特性が有効に働く領域の一つです。</span><span lang="en">Component-Based Development (CBD) is a foundational development approach in SimpleModeling. Separation of responsibilities, component reuse and composition, localized changes, and independent inspection and replacement provide broad benefits for software development and operation. Security is one of the areas in which these properties of CBD are particularly useful.</span>

<span lang="ja">CBDでは、Componentの内部実装をカプセル化し、外部へ公開するインターフェースを定めます。Component間の連携をProvided/Required契約へ集約し、依存関係を明示することで、外部から操作できる接点を限定し、内部への不用意なアクセスや意図しない結合を減らします。責務と接点が明確になるため、保護する対象と確認すべき経路も特定しやすくなります。これが、CBDの構造そのものがセキュリティに寄与する部分です。</span><span lang="en">CBD encapsulates each Component's internal implementation and defines the interfaces exposed to other components. Concentrating collaboration at Provided/Required contracts and making dependencies explicit limits exposed interaction points and reduces inadvertent access to internals and unintended coupling. Clear responsibilities and interaction points also make protected assets and paths requiring inspection easier to identify. These are the contributions that the structure of CBD itself makes to security.</span>

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFは、部品ごとの責務と権限規則を保ちながら、認証・認可・実行文脈・観測の機構を共通化します。独立した部品を、一貫した制御と運用へ接続する構成です。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF shares authentication, authorization, execution-context, and observability mechanisms while preserving each component’s responsibilities and authority rules. This connects independent components to consistent control and operation.</span>

<span lang="ja">CBDが区画と接点を定め、モデルと検査がその契約・必要権限を確認します。実行時には区画を越える呼出しを認可し、区画内部でも対象データと資源利用を制御します。「区画を作る構造」「区画を越える際の制御」「区画内部での制御」を共通機構で結び付けることで、独立性を保ちながら確認漏れと影響範囲を抑えます。この関係は、後述するティアごとの役割分担にも適用します。</span><span lang="en">CBD defines compartments and interfaces, while models and inspection establish their contracts and required authority. At runtime, calls crossing compartments are authorized, and target-data access and resource use are controlled inside each compartment. Shared mechanisms connect compartment structure, controls at crossings, and controls within compartments, preserving independence while reducing missed checks and limiting impact. The same relationship applies to the tier responsibilities described later.</span>

## Security Supported by Model-Driven Development｜モデル駆動開発が支えるセキュリティ

<span lang="ja">モデル駆動開発は、業務の概念や規則を実装技術より高い抽象度で記述し、その意味をプログラムの生成や実行へ結び付ける開発方式です。SimpleModelingでは、ドメイン知識に近い表現、共通のモデルに基づく設計と実装、複数の実装方式への展開などに活用しています。モデルとして意味を明示し、検査や変換に利用できるという特性は、セキュリティにも役立ちます。</span><span lang="en">Model-driven development describes business concepts and rules at a higher level of abstraction than implementation technologies and connects their meaning to program generation and execution. SimpleModeling uses it for domain-oriented expression, design and implementation grounded in shared models, and support for multiple implementation approaches. Making meaning explicit in models and available for inspection and transformation also benefits security.</span>

<span lang="ja">業務上の操作、入出力、状態、公開範囲、必要権限をモデルに明示すると、何を保護し、誰にどの操作を許すかを、個々の実装から切り離して確認できます。CMLはService/OperationやCapabilityなどの意味を保持し、契約の不足や不整合をモデルの検査とレビューの対象にします。業務上の意図とセキュリティ上の条件を同じモデルで扱うことで、設計段階で両者の対応を確認しやすくなります。</span><span lang="en">Explicit models of business operations, inputs and outputs, state, exposure, and required authority make it possible to review what is protected and who may perform which operations independently of individual implementations. CML retains semantics such as Service/Operation and Capability so that missing or inconsistent contracts can be examined through model checks and reviews. Representing business intent and security conditions in the same model makes their correspondence easier to assess during design.</span>

<span lang="ja">共通のモデルからScala/CNCF Container、軽量なTypeScript Cloud Function、API契約、CARメタデータ、配備制約などへ意味を投影することで、同じ条件を実装や設定ごとに書き直す箇所を減らせます。公開範囲や必要権限の変更も、モデルを起点に生成物へ反映し、その対応を検査できます。モデル駆動開発の一貫した変換が、対策の適用漏れや実装方式間の食い違いを減らします。</span><span lang="en">Projecting semantics from a shared model into Scala/CNCF Containers, lightweight TypeScript Cloud Functions, API contracts, CAR metadata, and deployment constraints reduces the places where the same conditions must be restated in code and configuration. Changes to exposure or required authority can originate in the model, flow into generated artifacts, and be checked for correspondence. Consistent model-driven transformation reduces omissions and discrepancies between implementation approaches.</span>

<span lang="ja">SimpleModelingでは、モデルに宣言した操作と必要権限に沿って、標準のAPIと実行経路を構成します。通常の生成物へ与える権限や低水準の操作を必要な範囲に絞ることで、実装が利用できる危険な操作の余地を小さくします。モデルに基づく生成は、共通の対策を繰り返し適用し、個々の業務処理でセキュリティ機構を組み立てる負担を減らす役割を持ちます。</span><span lang="en">SimpleModeling uses modeled operations and required authority to organize standard APIs and execution paths. Restricting the authority and low-level operations available to normal generated artifacts to what is needed reduces opportunities for dangerous implementation behavior. Model-based generation applies shared controls repeatedly and reduces the effort of assembling security mechanisms separately for each business operation.</span>

<span lang="ja">モデルが表す条件は、生成物と契約の対応を確認するテストやレビュー、配備時の受入れ判定、Textus/CNCFによる実行時の認可と資源制限へ引き継ぎます。モデル駆動開発が条件の明示・検査・一貫した変換を支え、実行基盤が実際の操作にその条件を適用します。Cloud FunctionとContainerのように実現方法が異なる場合も、この対応を維持することがセキュリティ上重要になります。</span><span lang="en">Conditions expressed in models are carried into tests and reviews of generated artifacts against their contracts, deployment admission, and runtime authorization and resource limits in Textus/CNCF. Model-driven development supports explicit conditions, inspection, and consistent transformation; the runtime applies those conditions to actual operations. Maintaining this correspondence across different realizations, including Cloud Functions and Containers, is important for security.</span>

## Connect Component Boundaries to Inspection, Execution, and Deployment｜Componentの境界を検査・実行・配備へ対応付ける

<span lang="ja">CBDが定めるのは、責務、内部データ、公開操作、依存関係の境界です。モデルに記述した境界をCARへまとめると、どの実装がどの契約と必要権限を持つかを、部品単位で検査できます。</span><span lang="en">CBD defines boundaries for responsibilities, internal data, public operations, and dependencies. Packaging those modeled boundaries in a CAR makes it possible to inspect which implementation carries which contracts and required authority as a component.</span>

<span lang="ja">実行時には、公開Operationの呼出しとUnitOfWorkによる対象データへのアクセスを共通の認可機構へ通し、資源利用をSandboxへ接続します。Componentごとの規則を標準経路の判定点へ対応付けることで、構造上の境界に実際の制限を適用します。</span><span lang="en">At runtime, public Operation calls and UnitOfWork access to target data pass through shared authorization mechanisms, while resource use is connected to the Sandbox. Mapping component-specific rules to checkpoints on standard paths applies enforceable restrictions to structural boundaries.</span>

<span lang="ja">配備では、Presentation・Application・Domainの責務と信頼境界に応じて、実行環境に与える権限と通信経路を定めます。別技術のPresentationからの要求も、サーバー側の検証・認可へ接続します。Componentの区分とプロセスやコンテナの隔離単位は一対一とは限らず、隔離や交換の範囲は配備構成として定めます。</span><span lang="en">Deployment defines execution-environment authority and communication paths according to Presentation, Application, and Domain responsibilities and trust boundaries. Requests from a Presentation tier using other technologies also enter server-side verification and authorization. Component boundaries need not map one-to-one to processes or containers; deployment configuration determines isolation and replacement scope.</span>

## Package Boundary Descriptions in Inspectable CARs｜境界の記述を検査可能なCARへまとめる

<span lang="ja">契約、必要権限、依存関係と実装を一つの配布単位へ集約すると、設計で定めた境界を、実際に利用する部品と対応付けて検査できます。CARはこの対応を保持し、CAR lint、CBD Review、受入れ判定が同じ配布物を対象に判断するための単位になります。検査対象を部品として持ち運べることが、検査結果に基づく再利用を支えます。</span><span lang="en">Bundling contracts, required authority, dependencies, and implementation in one distribution unit makes designed boundaries inspectable against the component that will actually be used. CAR retains this correspondence and provides a common artifact for CAR lint, CBD Review, and admission decisions. Carrying the inspection target as a component supports reuse based on assessment results.</span>

<span lang="ja">CARの識別情報と版を使い、モデル・実装・検査結果を同じ配布物へ対応付けます。配布後の検証と利用先の受入れは次章で説明します。</span><span lang="en">CAR identity and version associate models, implementation, and inspection results with the same distributable. Verification after distribution and admission at the destination are covered in the next chapter.</span>

<span lang="ja">CARにはComponent identity、Operation、dependency、Capability、implementation artifact、Subcomponent、documentation等の検査可能な情報を集約できます。</span><span lang="en">A CAR can aggregate inspectable information such as Component identity, Operations, dependencies, Capabilities, implementation artifacts, Subcomponents, and documentation.</span>

<span lang="ja">CARに記述したモデルと実装の対応を検査し、必要権限を配備先の方針と照合します。受け入れた権限を実行基盤へ適用することで、配布物の記述と実行上の境界をつなぎます。内容の妥当性の検査と、利用先で与える権限の判断は、それぞれの段階で行います。</span><span lang="en">The model-to-implementation correspondence described in a CAR is inspected, and required authority is checked against deployment policy. Applying admitted authority through the runtime connects artifact descriptions to execution boundaries. Content assessment and decisions about authority granted by the consuming environment take place at their respective stages.</span>

## Lint, Review and Admission｜Lint、レビュー、受入れ判定

<span lang="ja">CAR lintは機械的に判定できる構造や契約の違反を検出し、CBD Reviewは権限や依存関係を含む設計上の妥当性を確認します。判定の性質に応じて役割を分けます。</span><span lang="en">CAR lint detects mechanically decidable structural and contractual violations; CBD Review examines design suitability, including authority and dependencies. Their responsibilities follow the nature of the decision.</span>

<span lang="ja">コンパイル、テスト、AIレビュー、配布物の公開はいずれも、単独では実行権限を与えません。受入れ判定は、実行開始前に必要な契約と証拠を確認する独立した境界として扱います。</span><span lang="en">Compilation, tests, AI review, and artifact publication do not independently grant execution authority. Admission is a separate boundary that checks the required contracts and evidence before activation.</span>

<span lang="ja">静的検査、意味のレビュー、配備時の受入れは異なる判断を担当します。いずれか一つの成功を他の判断の代わりにせず、配備先で必要な権限だけを許可し、その制限を実行時にも維持します。</span><span lang="en">Static checks, semantic review, and deployment admission perform different judgments. Success in one does not replace the others. Admit only the authority needed in the deployment and preserve those limits during execution.</span>

## Align Inspection Scope with Shared Code and Self-Contained Artifacts｜共通実装と自己完結した配布物で検査対象を揃える

<span lang="ja">複数の実行環境で共通の実装を使うと、同じ処理に共通の検査を適用でき、対策の修正も同じソースへ集約できます。環境依存部分を薄いアダプターへ分けることで、プロバイダーごとに確認する範囲を限定します。検査対象の実装と配備情報を一つの配布物へまとめることは、何を検査し、何を配備するかを揃えるために役立ちます。</span><span lang="en">Sharing an implementation across execution environments enables common checks on the same processing and concentrates control fixes in the same source. Thin adapters isolate environment-specific behavior and bound what must be examined for each provider. Packaging the implementation under inspection with its deployment information helps align what is assessed with what is deployed.</span>

<span lang="ja">初期のCloud Function生成先はTypeScriptとします。プロバイダーに依存しない共通コアを一つ保ち、Local/Test、AWS、Googleの薄いアダプターが各実行環境へ接続します。各アダプターは共通のCloud Function ABIを使用します。</span><span lang="en">TypeScript is the initial Cloud Function generation target. One provider-neutral common core is maintained, with thin Local/Test, AWS, and Google adapters connecting it to each execution environment. The adapters use a shared Cloud Function ABI.</span>

<span lang="ja">各Cloud Function Subcomponent CARには共通TypeScript、対象アダプター、配備メタデータを含め、配布物を自己完結させます。共通コアの修正はソースで共有し、各アダプターとの組合せを検査して配布・更新します。共通コードの重複除去だけを目的とする別のCloud Function CARは設けません。</span><span lang="en">Each Cloud Function Subcomponent CAR contains the shared TypeScript, target adapter, and deployment metadata as a self-contained artifact. Common-core fixes are shared at source level, tested with each adapter, and distributed as updates. No separate Cloud Function CAR is introduced solely to deduplicate shared code.</span>

## Check Security Behavior Across Realizations with Shared Executable Specifications｜共通の動く仕様書で実現方式間のセキュリティ動作を確かめる

<span lang="ja">同じ論理OperationをContainerとCloud Functionで実現する場合、共通の動く仕様書を使って、入力の検査、認可、拒否時の応答や状態変更など、外部から観測できる契約を確認します。実現方式の違いによって、本来拒否すべき操作が許可されたり、拒否した処理が状態を変更したりする食い違いを検出するための検証です。</span><span lang="en">When Containers and Cloud Functions realize the same logical Operation, shared executable specifications check externally observable contracts, including input checks, authorization, rejection responses, and state changes. These tests aim to detect discrepancies such as one realization accepting an operation that should be rejected or changing state after rejecting it.</span>

<span lang="ja">Local/Testは共通のCloud Function ABIを実行するアダプターとして、共通コアと境界の振る舞いをプロバイダー固有の環境から切り離して確認できるようにします。条件を揃えて繰り返し検証できることが、生成やアダプターの変更によるセキュリティ動作の後退を早い段階で検出する助けになります。</span><span lang="en">As an adapter implementing the common Cloud Function ABI, Local/Test allows checks of the common core and boundary behavior independently of provider-specific environments. Repeatable checks under controlled conditions help detect security-behavior regressions caused by generator or adapter changes early.</span>

<span lang="ja">検証は、共通コアとLocal/Testでの反復可能な確認を先に行い、Domain連携、Active/Standbyやキャッシュ、プロバイダー・アダプターの契約へ広げます。最後に実クラウドで配備権限と到達経路を確認します。</span><span lang="en">Verification starts with repeatable checks of the shared core and Local/Test, then covers Domain integration, Active/Standby and caches, and provider-adapter contracts. Tests in the actual cloud finally check deployment authority and reachable paths.</span>

<span lang="ja">共通の動く仕様書はOperationの契約を、アダプター契約の検査は実行環境との接点を確認します。クラウド固有の権限設定や実際の到達経路は、配備先の受入れ試験で確認します。この分担により、再現可能な検証を繰り返しながら、実環境でしか確認できない条件も検査対象に含めます。</span><span lang="en">Shared executable specifications check Operation contracts, while adapter-contract checks examine interfaces with execution environments. Deployment acceptance tests check cloud-specific permission settings and actual reachable paths. This division combines repeatable verification with checks of conditions observable only in the real environment.</span>

## Control AI Development Risks by Separating the Actor from Its Artifacts｜生成主体と成果物を分けてAI開発のリスクを制御する

<span lang="ja">AI開発では、開発作業を行う主体と、生成された成果物を分けて管理できます。AIが使うツールや資源の権限をSandboxで限定すれば、開発中の誤判断が及ぼす範囲を絞れます。生成物を通常のモデル・CAR・レビュー・受入れの経路へ通すことで、アプリケーションへ持ち込む欠陥を検査できます。この二つを組み合わせ、作業中の作用と成果物の品質をそれぞれ制御します。</span><span lang="en">AI development allows the development actor and its generated artifacts to be managed separately. Restricting the actor's tool and resource authority through Sandbox limits the effects of misjudgments during development. Routing generated artifacts through the ordinary model, CAR, review, and admission process checks defects before introduction into applications. Together, these mechanisms control development-time effects and artifact quality separately.</span>

<span lang="ja">sm-workflowは開発工程と検証結果の積み上げを管理し、CAR lintとCBD Reviewが生成物の機械的な違反と設計上の問題を確認します。検査結果を修正と再検証へ戻すことで、生成AIの自己評価に加えて、共通の基準による確認結果を採用判断へ渡します。</span><span lang="en">sm-workflow manages development stages and accumulated verification results, while CAR lint and CBD Review check mechanical violations and design issues in generated artifacts. Feeding findings into correction and revalidation provides adoption decisions with evidence from shared criteria beyond the generating AI's own assessment.</span>

<span lang="ja">高い権限を伴う操作、標準経路から外れる例外、重要な受入れ・リリース判断には、人間による確認を組み込みます。自動検査で得た結果と、業務上許容できる影響や例外の判断を接続する役割です。</span><span lang="en">Human review is included for high-authority operations, exceptions to standard paths, and consequential admission and release decisions. It connects automated findings with judgments about acceptable business effects and exceptions.</span>

<span lang="ja">成果物の評価は、作成者がAIか人間かにかかわらず、契約への適合と検証結果に基づきます。共通の検査を適用することで、生成方法が変わっても同じ採用基準を維持します。</span><span lang="en">Artifact assessment is based on contract conformance and verification results, whether the author is AI or human. Shared checks preserve the same adoption criteria across generation methods.</span>

# Delivering Assessed Artifacts Through Trusted Paths｜検査した成果物を信頼できる経路で届ける

<span lang="ja">モデルと実装の検査結果を利用先へ引き継ぐには、検査した内容と実際に配備する内容を対応付ける必要があります。電子署名は配布元と内容を確認する手段となり、Component Repositoryは配布・取得の共通経路となります。利用先のAdmissionは、その成果物が自分の配備条件と権限方針に適合するかを判定します。</span><span lang="en">Carrying assessment results to consumers requires relating the assessed contents to what is deployed. Signatures establish publisher and content identity, Component Repositories provide a shared distribution path, and consumer-side admission checks suitability for local deployment conditions and authority policies.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/artifact-trust-path-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/artifact-trust-path-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">検査、署名、Repository、Admission、実行時制御は異なる判断を担当します。図は設計上の接続を示し、個別機能の提供状況は本文で扱います。</span><span lang="en">Assessment, signatures, repositories, admission, and runtime controls make distinct decisions. This is the architectural relationship; availability is discussed in the text.</span>

<span lang="ja">部品の契約と検査結果を配布先まで引き継ぎ、そこで許可する権限を定めます。この受入れ結果を次章の実行時制御へ接続することで、検査済み部品の再利用と利用先ごとの権限制限を両立します。</span><span lang="en">Component contracts and inspection results are carried to the destination, where granted authority is determined. Connecting admission to the runtime controls in the next chapter combines reuse of assessed components with destination-specific authority limits.</span>

## Verify the Publisher and CAR Content with Digital Signatures｜電子署名で配布元とCARの内容を確認する

<span lang="ja">CAR lintとCBD Reviewは、コンポーネントの契約、権限、依存関係、実装や設計の妥当性を検査します。電子署名は、信頼する提供者の鍵による署名であることと、署名後にCARの内容が変更されていないことを確認します。検査と署名を組み合わせることで、所定の検証を経た配布物を識別して利用するための根拠が揃います。</span><span lang="en">CAR lint and CBD Review assess contracts, authority, dependencies, implementation, and design. Digital signatures establish that a trusted publisher key signed the CAR and that its content has not changed since signing. Combining assessment and signatures provides a basis for identifying and using the artifact that underwent the required checks.</span>

<span lang="ja">検査結果は対象CARの識別情報、バージョン、内容へ対応付けて管理します。署名は完成したCAR全体を対象にし、署名後の再圧縮や差し替えを同じ検証済み配布物として扱いません。変更したCARについては、内容に対応する検査結果と署名を用意します。電子署名そのものは、検査を実施した事実やコードの安全性を証明するものではありません。</span><span lang="en">Associate assessment results with the CAR identity, version, and content. Sign the completed CAR as a whole, and do not treat recompressed or replaced content as the same verified artifact. Changed CARs need corresponding assessment results and signatures. A signature alone does not prove that checks occurred or that the code is safe.</span>

<span lang="ja">利用者は信頼するRepositoryの起点となる鍵を設定し、その起点から検証できる提供者の鍵情報を利用します。署名が数学的に正しいことに加え、その鍵が対象namespaceへの署名を許可された有効な鍵であることを確認します。CARと一緒に届いた鍵を、同梱されているという理由だけで信頼しません。</span><span lang="en">Consumers configure a Repository trust root and use publisher-key information verifiable from it. In addition to cryptographic validity, check that the key is valid and authorized for the CAR namespace. A key delivered with a CAR is not trusted merely because it is bundled with it.</span>

<span lang="ja">ここで説明するのは、署名と内容検査を組み合わせた利用モデルです。既存の採用済み配布仕様では署名は任意であり、未署名CARもチェックサム検証後に取得できます。未署名CARを署名確認済みとは扱わず、存在する署名の取得・検証に失敗した場合は未署名へ切り替えて受け入れません。署名・取得検証は開発予定の契約として整理されており、本稿で実装完了を主張するものではありません。</span><span lang="en">This section describes a use model combining signatures and content assessment. The adopted general distribution specification makes signing optional and permits unsigned CAR retrieval after checksum verification. An unsigned CAR is not signature-verified, and a failed retrieval or verification of a present signature must not fall back to unsigned acceptance. Signature and retrieval verification are planned contracts; this guide does not assert implementation completion.</span>

## Distribute and Use Assessed Components Through Component Repository｜Component Repositoryを通じて検証済みコンポーネントを配布・利用する

<span lang="ja">配布側では、モデル・契約・実装をCARへまとめ、CAR lintで機械的な違反を検査し、CBD Reviewで権限や依存関係、設計の意味を確認します。署名付きの配布では、その検査対象に対応する完成CARへ署名します。Component RepositoryはCARの版、依存関係、検証結果の参照、署名と提供者の情報を対応付けて配布する構成とします。</span><span lang="en">The publisher packages models, contracts, and code into a CAR, uses CAR lint for mechanical violations, and uses CBD Review for authority, dependency, and design judgments. Signed distribution signs the completed CAR corresponding to that assessment. The Component Repository distribution model associates CAR versions and dependencies with assessment references, signatures, and publisher information.</span>

<span lang="ja">取得側はCARを一時領域へダウンロードし、完成した取得物のチェックサムと、署名がある場合は信頼する鍵による署名を検証します。成功したそのCARを利用可能なキャッシュへ登録し、展開・ローディングへ進みます。検証後に別のファイルを取り直して検証済みとして扱いません。</span><span lang="en">The consumer downloads a CAR into temporary storage and verifies the completed download against its checksum and, when signed, a trusted-key signature. Those accepted CAR bytes enter usable cache before extraction and loading. A different file fetched afterward is not treated as the verified artifact.</span>

<span lang="ja">利用者は、出所が確認でき、所定のCAR lint・CBD Reviewを経た版を選択できます。チェックサムは取得時の破損検出、署名は配布元と内容の確認、lintとReviewは内容の検査を担当します。この分担をRepositoryで管理することで、利用者が個々の部品の検証状況を調べ、再利用の判断へつなげられます。</span><span lang="en">Consumers can select versions with verified provenance and the required CAR lint and CBD Review results. Checksums detect download corruption, signatures verify provenance and content, and lint and review assess that content. Repository management makes these distinct facts available for component-reuse decisions.</span>

<span lang="ja">取得・検証したCARを、利用先でそのまま無制限に実行するわけではありません。必要権限、依存CAR、runtimeや更新の互換性を配備方針と照合し、許可した範囲を認可とSandboxへ適用します。利用中の依存関係や脆弱性情報も更新判断へつなぎ、過去の検証結果を将来のすべての構成に対する保証としません。</span><span lang="en">Retrieval and verification do not authorize unrestricted execution. Compare required authority, dependent CARs, runtime requirements, and update compatibility with deployment policy, and apply admitted scope through authorization and Sandbox. Dependency and vulnerability information informs later updates; past assessment is not assurance for every future configuration.</span>

# Covering Required Protection Along Execution Paths｜必要な保護範囲を実行経路に沿って揃える

<span lang="ja">受け入れたComponentを動かす際は、共通の認証・認可経路を使い、対象Component・Domainの規則を適用します。外部要求の受入れ、操作とデータの認可、入力・出力の保護、資源制限は、それぞれ異なる境界を担当します。</span><span lang="en">Admitted components run through shared authentication and authorization paths that apply the target Component or Domain’s rules. External-request admission, operation and data authorization, input and output protection, and resource limits each address a different boundary.</span>

<span lang="ja">以下では、まず脅威と対策の対応を一覧で示し、次に各境界の構成と処理を説明します。個々の技術の名前だけでなく、どの情報で判断し、どの実行経路に適用し、何を次の機構へ渡すかを確認することで、対策同士の接続を理解できます。</span><span lang="en">The following sections first map threats to controls and then explain each boundary's structure and processing. Identifying decision inputs, enforcement paths, and information passed to the next mechanism makes the connections between controls technically understandable.</span>

## Threats, Combined Controls, Assumptions, and Limits｜脅威・対策の組合せ・前提と限界

<span lang="ja">一覧では、対策の名称とともに組合せによる働きと前提・限界を示します。各行を独立した保証とせず、対応する章の説明と合わせて確認します。</span><span lang="en">The mapping identifies combined behavior as well as control names, assumptions, and limits. Read each row with its chapter rather than as an independent guarantee.</span>

<span lang="ja">保護対象とセキュリティ機構の対応</span><span lang="en">Protection targets and security mechanisms</span>

| <span lang="ja">保護対象・脅威</span><span lang="en">Protection target / threat</span> | <span lang="ja">適用する機構と保護</span><span lang="en">Mechanisms and protection</span> | <span lang="ja">前提・補完する対策</span><span lang="en">Conditions and complementary controls</span> |
|---|---|---|
| <span lang="ja">Domainへの不正アクセス</span><span lang="en">Unauthorized Domain access</span> | <span lang="ja">認証状態をSecuritySubjectへ正規化し、Operationの呼出しとUnitOfWorkでの対象Entityアクセスを別々に認可します。Sandboxが資源利用を制限します。</span><span lang="en">Normalize authentication state into SecuritySubject and separately authorize Operation invocation and target-Entity access at UnitOfWork; Sandbox limits resources.</span> | <span lang="ja">呼出し許可だけでは対象データへの権限になりません。主体・対象・状況と失効の扱いを確認します。</span><span lang="en">Invocation permission does not grant target-data rights. Check subject, target, context, and revocation behavior.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">公開Cloud Functionの侵害</span><span lang="en">Compromised public Cloud Function</span> | <span lang="ja">公開側の機能と権限を縮小し、Domain DBへ直接アクセスさせず、各Domainで認可します。</span><span lang="en">Reduce public-tier features and authority, withhold direct Domain DB access, and authorize per Domain.</span> | <span lang="ja">許可された経路の悪用は残り得るため、対象別認可と観測・失効を併用します。</span><span lang="en">Permitted paths can still be abused; combine target-specific authorization with observation and revocation.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">DDoS・過負荷</span><span lang="en">DDoS and overload</span> | <span lang="ja">エッジ対策、モデルの入力制約、安価な事前検査、下流同時実行数の制限を組み合わせます。</span><span lang="en">Combine edge controls, model input constraints, cheap prechecks, and downstream concurrency limits.</span> | <span lang="ja">入力が妥当でも大量到来は起こります。回線や提供基盤の容量も別途扱います。</span><span lang="en">Valid requests can still arrive in volume. Network and provider capacity require separate treatment.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">SQLインジェクション</span><span lang="en">SQL injection</span> | <span lang="ja">型付きRepository/DataStoreを通常経路にし、raw SQLを例外検査へ回し、実行主体の権限を限定します。</span><span lang="en">Use typed Repository/DataStore paths, inspect raw-SQL escape hatches, and limit executor authority.</span> | <span lang="ja">型の宣言だけで任意のSQL実装が安全になるとは扱いません。</span><span lang="en">Type declarations alone do not make arbitrary SQL implementations safe.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">XSS・CSRF・マスアサインメント</span><span lang="en">XSS, CSRF, and mass assignment</span> | <span lang="ja">出力文脈別のレンダリング、更新Operationと入口のCSRF方針、宣言入力への束縛を組み合わせます。</span><span lang="en">Combine context-aware rendering, mutation Operations and ingress CSRF policy, and declared input binding.</span> | <span lang="ja">各対策は別の経路を担当します。例外出力や入力経路も検査します。</span><span lang="en">These controls cover distinct paths; inspect exceptional output and input paths as well.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">資源の不正利用</span><span lang="en">Unauthorized resource use</span> | <span lang="ja">Componentの必要権限をモデル化し、受入れ時に確認し、SandboxとExecutionLimitsで適用します。</span><span lang="en">Model Component authority needs, check them at admission, and enforce them through Sandbox and ExecutionLimits.</span> | <span lang="ja">制限を迂回できる直接経路を残さないことが前提になります。</span><span lang="en">This depends on excluding direct paths that bypass enforcement.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Credential・Secretの漏洩</span><span lang="en">Credential or Secret disclosure</span> | <span lang="ja">分類に基づいて保持を減らし、外部へ委譲し、アクセス権限とlog/traceへの出力を制限します。</span><span lang="en">Minimize retention by classification, delegate externally, and limit access and log/trace output.</span> | <span lang="ja">必要な参照や個人情報の保護は残ります。委譲先との境界も確認します。</span><span lang="en">Necessary references and personal data still need protection; verify the provider boundary too.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">実行環境の侵害</span><span lang="en">Runtime compromise</span> | <span lang="ja">最小権限で影響を限定し、観測・失効・隔離を経て不変の成果物から環境を交換します。</span><span lang="en">Limit impact through least authority, then observe, revoke, isolate, and replace from immutable artifacts.</span> | <span lang="ja">交換だけでは過去の漏洩や不正更新を取り消せません。</span><span lang="en">Replacement alone does not undo past disclosure or unauthorized mutations.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">待機系・復旧経路の不備</span><span lang="en">Defective standby or recovery paths</span> | <span lang="ja">通常の読取りと定期交代で準備確認、昇格、drain、キャッシュ再構築を継続して動かします。</span><span lang="en">Exercise readiness, promotion, draining, and cache rebuilding through ordinary reads and regular rotation.</span> | <span lang="ja">交換可能性と永続状態の正しさを分けて確認します。</span><span lang="en">Check replaceability separately from persistent-state correctness.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">配布物・生成コードの欠陥</span><span lang="en">Artifact and generated-code defects</span> | <span lang="ja">CAR lintとCBD Reviewで内容を検査し、電子署名とComponent Repositoryで検査対象・提供者・配布物を対応付け、利用先で受け入れます。</span><span lang="en">Assess content with CAR lint and CBD Review, link assessed artifacts and publishers to distributed CARs through signatures and Component Repository, and admit them locally.</span> | <span lang="ja">署名だけでは内容検査の実施を証明しません。未署名CARの扱いと配布検証の開発状況を区別し、実行権限は利用先で限定します。</span><span lang="en">A signature alone does not prove assessment. Distinguish unsigned treatment and verification implementation status, and limit authority in the consuming environment.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">AIの誤判断・ツール利用の暴走</span><span lang="en">AI misjudgment and tool misuse</span> | <span lang="ja">生成物の検査に加え、AI自身のツール権限をSandboxで限定し、重要な判断に人間が関与します。</span><span lang="en">Inspect generated artifacts, constrain the AI actor's tool authority through Sandbox, and involve humans in consequential decisions.</span> | <span lang="ja">指示や自己評価だけを強制機構や独立した証拠と扱いません。</span><span lang="en">Instructions and self-assessment are neither enforcement nor independent evidence.</span> |
| <span lang="ja">過剰な防御機構</span><span lang="en">Excessive defensive machinery</span> | <span lang="ja">脅威と必要権限を設計レビューで確認し、既存の制限・観測・復旧の経路を利用します。</span><span lang="en">Review threats and required authority and use established constraint, observation, and recovery paths.</span> | <span lang="ja">複雑さを減らすことを理由に、必要な検証や防御を省きません。</span><span lang="en">Reducing complexity does not justify omitting necessary checks or defenses.</span> |

## Limit the Admission of External Requests｜外部要求を受け入れる範囲を限定する

<span lang="ja">外部要求の受付では、公開側の検査や処理が内部の保護を迂回しない構成が必要です。</span><span lang="en">External-request admission needs a structure in which public-tier checks and processing do not bypass internal protection.</span>

<span lang="ja">以下では、ティアごとの信頼境界、Cloud Function Firstによる公開処理の限定、過負荷を内部へ伝えない受入れ制御を順に説明します。</span><span lang="en">The following sections explain tier-specific trust boundaries, the restriction of public processing through Cloud Function First, and admission control that limits propagation of overload.</span>

<span lang="ja">これらは、公開する機能と権限の範囲、および内部へ渡す処理量をそれぞれ制御します。</span><span lang="en">These mechanisms control the scope of exposed functionality and authority, and the amount of work forwarded internally.</span>

<span lang="ja">受け入れた要求に対する操作・対象データの認可は、後続のDomain側の判定へ接続します。</span><span lang="en">Authorization of admitted requests against operations and target data is connected to subsequent decisions in the Domain.</span>

### Three-Tier Trust Architecture｜三つのティアの信頼アーキテクチャ

<span lang="ja">ティアは実行・配備上の区分です。本書では、利用者との対話を担当するPresentation tierをUIティアとも呼びます。Application tierは外部要求の受付と業務操作の組合せを、Domain tierは業務規則と状態の管理を担当します。</span><span lang="en">A tier is an execution and deployment division. This guide also calls the Presentation tier, which handles user interaction, the UI tier. The Application tier receives external requests and coordinates business operations, while the Domain tier manages business rules and state.</span>

<span lang="ja">Presentation tierは、TypeScript／Node.jsやFlutterなど、Textusとは異なる技術で構築できます。Textusのセキュリティ機構を直接利用できない構成も想定し、Presentationを信頼の前提にしないZero Trustの境界を設けます。クライアント側の検査や画面上の操作制限は、サーバー側の入力検証や認可の代わりにはしません。</span><span lang="en">The Presentation tier can be built with technologies other than Textus, such as TypeScript/Node.js or Flutter. The architecture accommodates clients that cannot use Textus security mechanisms directly and establishes a Zero Trust boundary that does not assume trust in the Presentation tier. Client-side checks and screen-level operation restrictions do not replace server-side input validation or authorization.</span>

<span lang="ja">Application tierは外部要求の検証と業務操作の組合せを担当し、Domainの公開APIを通して連携します。Cloud Function Firstで処理を小さく構成し、Domainの内部データへ直接到達する権限を持たせません。具体的な機能・権限の絞り方は次節で説明します。</span><span lang="en">The Application tier verifies external requests and coordinates business operations through public Domain APIs. Cloud Function First keeps execution units small, without authority to access internal Domain data directly. The next section explains how functionality and authority are restricted.</span>

<span lang="ja">Domain tierは、Applicationから渡された認証状態と呼出し元を検証・解決し、自分の規則で操作を認可します。Operationの呼出し可否に加え、UnitOfWorkで対象Entityへのアクセスを判定し、業務規則と状態遷移の条件を適用します。さらにSandboxで利用できる資源と消費量を制限します。Applicationからの呼出しであることや、Domain内部の処理であることだけでは、無制限の権限を与えません。</span><span lang="en">The Domain tier verifies and resolves authentication state and caller identity received from the Application and authorizes operations under its own rules. In addition to permission to invoke an Operation, UnitOfWork checks access to target Entities, and business rules and state-transition conditions are applied. The Sandbox further limits accessible resources and consumption. Calls from the Application or execution inside the Domain do not by themselves confer unrestricted authority.</span>

<span lang="ja">ティア間では責務・権限・到達経路を限定し、Domain内部では共通機構によって操作・対象データ・資源の規則を適用します。要求が外部から内部へ進んでも、許可範囲は無条件に広がりません。Presentationの技術選択、ApplicationのCloud Function Firstと機能・権限の限定、Domain内部の制御を組み合わせることで、システム全体のセキュリティ強度を支えます。</span><span lang="en">Between tiers, responsibilities, authority, and reachable paths are bounded; within the Domain, shared mechanisms apply rules for operations, target data, and resources. Moving a request from outside to inside does not automatically widen its permissions. Combining Presentation technology choice, Cloud Function First with bounded Application functionality and authority, and internal Domain controls supports the security of the system as a whole.</span>

<span lang="ja">ティアごとの責務と境界</span><span lang="en">Tier Responsibilities and Boundaries</span>

| <span lang="ja">ティア</span><span lang="en">Tier</span> | <span lang="ja">担当する保護</span><span lang="en">Protection responsibility</span> | <span lang="ja">次の境界へ渡すもの</span><span lang="en">Handoff to the next boundary</span> |
|---|---|---|
| <span lang="ja">Presentation</span><span lang="en">Presentation</span> | <span lang="ja">UI基盤の安全な描画と操作支援</span><span lang="en">Safe UI rendering and interaction</span> | <span lang="ja">サーバーが検証する入力・認証情報</span><span lang="en">Inputs and authentication information for server verification</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Application</span><span lang="en">Application</span> | <span lang="ja">外部要求の検証、操作の組合せ、機能・権限の限定</span><span lang="en">Request verification, coordination, limited functions and authority</span> | <span lang="ja">Domainの公開APIへの要求・認証参照・観測文脈</span><span lang="en">Public Domain API request, authentication reference, observation context</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Domain</span><span lang="en">Domain</span> | <span lang="ja">Operation・Entity認可、業務規則、資源制御</span><span lang="en">Operation/Entity authorization, business rules, resource controls</span> | <span lang="ja">認可された結果と監査・観測記録</span><span lang="en">Authorized results and audit/observation records</span> |

### Limit Public-Tier Impact with Small Cloud Functions and Bounded Authority｜小さなCloud Functionと権限の限定で公開部分の影響範囲を絞る

<span lang="ja">Applicationティアの処理は、コンテナまたはCloud Functionとして実行します。Cloud Functionは、クラウドの実行基盤が要求やイベントに応じて呼び出す処理単位です。</span><span lang="en">Processing in the Application tier runs in a container or as a Cloud Function. A Cloud Function is a unit of processing invoked by a cloud execution platform in response to a request or event.</span>

<span lang="ja">Cloud Function Firstは、コストと拡張性に加え、公開側の機能と権限を小さく保つための選択です。Operation単位の処理へ必要な権限だけを付与し、Domain DB、CAR Runtime、任意のファイル操作などの不要な機能を持たせません。Domainへは公開APIを通して接続し、Domain側で操作と対象データを認可します。Cloud Functionの処理単位と、この権限・接続先の限定を組み合わせることで、Application側の欠陥や侵害が及ぼせる範囲を抑えます。</span><span lang="en">Cloud Function First is chosen for cost and scalability and for keeping public-tier functionality and authority small. Each Operation-sized function receives only the authority it needs, without unnecessary facilities such as Domain DB access, a CAR Runtime, or arbitrary file operations. It connects to the Domain through public APIs, where operations and target-data access are authorized. Combining the Cloud Function execution unit with these authority and destination restrictions limits the effects of defects or compromise in the Application tier.</span>

<span lang="ja">CMLでは通常のService/Operationとしてアプリケーションをモデル化し、クラウド・プロバイダーの概念を基本要素にはしません。生成時には全Application Operationを含む完全なCNCF Containerを用意し、そのうちCloud Functionに適したOperationを追加のCloud Functionとしての実現へ投影します。</span><span lang="en">Applications are modeled in CML as ordinary Services and Operations; cloud-provider concepts are not fundamental modeling elements. Generation produces a complete CNCF Container containing all Application Operations and additionally projects cloud-function-eligible Operations into Cloud Function realizations.</span>

<span lang="ja">Cloud Functionとして表現できるかという候補判定と、特定プロバイダーへ配備できるかという判定は区別します。Cloud Functionに適さない処理は完全なContainer実現を利用し、その場合もApplicationとDomainの責務・権限の境界を維持します。実行形式の選択が変わっても、同じ業務契約と権限方針を適用します。</span><span lang="en">Cloud Function candidacy and eligibility for deployment to a particular provider are separate decisions. Operations unsuitable for Cloud Functions use the complete Container realization while retaining the responsibility and authority boundaries between Application and Domain. The same business contracts and authority policies apply across choices of execution form.</span>

<span lang="ja">Cloud Functionは性能要件に応じて実行環境を再利用し、初期化の負担や応答時間を抑えます。呼出しごとの処理時間と実行環境の寿命を分けて捉え、呼出し間の状態の隔離と、不要になった環境の廃棄を組み合わせます。長時間維持するコンテナよりも実行環境が短命に管理される構成では、侵害状態の持続時間を抑える効果を期待できます。この効果は実行基盤の隔離・再利用・廃棄の方針に依存するため、Applicationティアではそれらの特性と応答性能を合わせて評価します。</span><span lang="en">Cloud Functions reuse execution environments to meet performance requirements, reducing initialization overhead and response latency. Invocation duration is distinguished from environment lifetime, combining isolation of state between invocations with disposal of environments when no longer needed. Where environments are managed with shorter lifetimes than long-running containers, this can reduce the persistence of compromise. The effect depends on the platform's isolation, reuse, and disposal policies, which are evaluated alongside response performance in the Application tier.</span>

### Cloud Functions in the Application tier as a Security and Availability Boundary｜セキュリティと可用性の境界としてのApplicationティアのCloud Function

<span lang="ja">検査は、プロバイダー側のエッジ・WAF・レート制限・bot対策、要求の検証、明白なcredential不正の拒否、Cloud Functionへの受入れ、本人確認の解決、Domainでの認可、Domain Operationの順に、安価な処理から高価な処理へ進めます。この順序と下流の同時実行数の制限を組み合わせ、公開側の負荷がUser ManagementやDomainへそのまま流れ込むことを抑えます。</span><span lang="en">Checks proceed from inexpensive to expensive processing: provider edge/WAF/rate/bot controls, request validation, rejection of obviously invalid credentials, Cloud Function admission, identity resolution, Domain authorization, and finally the Domain Operation. Combining this ordering with bounded downstream concurrency limits the propagation of public-facing load into User Management and Domains.</span>

<span lang="ja">モデルの型・長さ・件数等の入力制約は、制約違反の要求をパラメータ検査で拒否し、不要な内部処理やメモリ消費を抑えます。形式上は妥当な要求の大量到来は別の問題であり、レート制限と下流の受入れ制御で扱います。</span><span lang="en">Model constraints on types, lengths, and counts reject violating requests during parameter validation and reduce unnecessary internal work and memory consumption. Large volumes of otherwise valid requests are a separate issue, handled by rate limits and downstream admission.</span>

<span lang="ja">これらは資源を保護するための受入れ境界です。通過した要求についても、User Managementによる本人確認とDomainごとの認可を続けて行います。</span><span lang="en">These controls form a resource-protection admission boundary. Requests that pass it still require identity resolution by User Management and authorization by each Domain.</span>

## Apply Authority from Identity Resolution Through Execution｜本人確認から業務実行まで権限を適用する

<span lang="ja">Applicationで受け入れた要求も、Domainでは主体・操作・対象に応じて認可します。Textus側で認証状態の表現と判定機構を共通化し、各Component・Domainの規則を適用する構成です。</span><span lang="en">Requests admitted by the Application are still authorized in the Domain according to subject, operation, and target. Textus shares authentication-state representation and decision mechanisms while applying each Component or Domain’s own rules.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/authorization-two-boundaries-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/authorization-two-boundaries-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">認証した主体を二つの認可境界へ引き継ぎます。Entityの基本権限と用途別規則を共通機構で評価し、許可・拒否の結果を記録へつなぎます。</span><span lang="en">The authenticated subject passes through two authorization boundaries. Shared mechanisms evaluate Entity baseline permissions and application-specific rules and connect allowed/denied outcomes to records.</span>

<span lang="ja">主体に対応する認証プロバイダーが本人・呼出し元を確認し、内部の認証状態とSecuritySubjectへ正規化します。認可は、Operationを呼び出せるかと、処理中に対象Entityへアクセスできるかの二段階で行います。Cloud Function連携のAuthHandleはこの共通経路へ認証状態を渡し、Sandboxは実行資源の範囲を制限します。</span><span lang="en">A subject-specific authentication provider verifies the user or caller and normalizes the result into internal authentication state and SecuritySubject. Authorization has two stages: permission to invoke an Operation and permission to access target Entities during execution. AuthHandle carries authentication state into this common path for Cloud Function coordination, while Sandbox limits runtime resources.</span>

<span lang="ja">認証で主体を確立し、SimpleEntityの基本情報と既定の権限を共通の判定経路へ渡すことで、基本的な保護を適用します。用途別の規則も同じ経路で評価するため、認可手法を増やしても各部品へ別々の判定機構を実装する必要はありません。</span><span lang="en">Authentication establishes the subject, and shared decision paths use SimpleEntity metadata and default permissions to apply baseline protection. Application-specific rules use the same paths, so additional authorization methods do not require separate decision engines in each component.</span>

<span lang="ja">許可範囲の中でも、入力の扱いやSQL・HTMLの生成に欠陥があれば問題は起こり得ます。次章ではモデルと標準APIによってその発生を減らし、例外経路を検査へつなぎます。</span><span lang="en">Defects in input handling or SQL and HTML construction can still cause problems within admitted authority. The next chapter reduces those defects through models and standard APIs and connects exceptional paths to inspection.</span>

### Operate Independent Components Through Shared Authentication and Authorization｜独立したコンポーネントを共通の認証・認可で運用する

<span lang="ja">コンポーネント化しても、認証状態の受渡しや認可の適用方法が部品ごとに異なると、それらを接続し、一貫して運用するための個別対応が必要になります。Textus/CNCFでは、主体の表現、認可の判定機構、実行文脈、監査・観測の経路を共通化します。</span><span lang="en">Componentization still requires custom integration and operational coordination when components differ in how they transfer authentication state and apply authorization. Textus/CNCF shares the representation of subjects, authorization mechanisms, execution context, and audit and observability paths.</span>

<span lang="ja">共通化するのは機構です。各Component・Domainは、自分が公開する操作と管理するデータについて、必要権限や業務上の許可条件を定めます。認証された主体を共通の形式で受け取り、それぞれの規則で判定するため、連携先で認証済みであることを、そのまま自分の操作やデータへの許可にはしません。</span><span lang="en">The mechanisms are shared. Each Component or Domain defines the authority and business conditions required for its public operations and managed data. It receives an authenticated subject in a common form and evaluates its own rules; authentication or permission elsewhere does not by itself authorize access to its operations or data.</span>

<span lang="ja">この構成により、部品ごとに認証処理や認可の接続コードを作る負担を減らし、異なる入口や連携先でも共通の判定手順を適用できます。認証状態の失効を各経路へ反映し、主体・操作・対象・判定結果を関連付けて観測することで、区画ごとの独立性を保ちながらシステム全体を管理・運用します。</span><span lang="en">This arrangement reduces per-component authentication implementations and authorization integration code while applying common decision procedures across entry points and collaborating components. Propagating revocation of authentication state and correlating subjects, operations, targets, and decisions supports system-wide management and operation while preserving component independence.</span>

### Authentication Subjects and Provider Responsibilities｜認証する主体と認証プロバイダーの役割

<span lang="ja">認証は、要求を行う主体の識別情報と認証の事実を確立します。人間の利用者だけでなく、呼出し元のサービスやサブシステムも対象になります。利用者を代行する呼出しでは、利用者の識別と呼出し元サービスの識別を区別します。</span><span lang="en">Authentication establishes a requesting subject's identity and authentication facts. Subjects include human users, services, and subsystems. A call made on a user's behalf distinguishes the user's identity from the identity of the calling service.</span>

<span lang="ja">CNCFは入口で認証情報を受け取り、配備設定に従って主体に対応する認証プロバイダーを選びます。人間のアカウント、資格情報、セッションはtextus-user-accountなどの人間向けプロバイダーが扱い、サービス認証は対応する別のプロバイダーの責務とします。CNCFは成功した認証結果を共通の実行コンテキストへ取り込みます。</span><span lang="en">CNCF receives authentication input at ingress and selects a subject-specific provider according to deployment configuration. Human-oriented providers such as textus-user-account manage human accounts, credentials, and sessions; service authentication belongs to a corresponding separate provider. CNCF incorporates successful results into the common execution context.</span>

<span lang="ja">外部認証では、プロバイダー・アダプターが方式に応じた署名、発行者、利用先、有効期限、コールバック状態などを検証します。検証済みの外部主体は、プロバイダーと安定した主体識別子の組で内部UserAccountへ対応付けます。メールアドレスだけによる誤った結合を避け、外部トークンは内部セッションやDomain権限へ直接置き換えません。未検証の認証情報、利用が許可されていない方式、未登録のアダプターは認証失敗とします。各方式の利用可否は、提供済みアダプターと配備設定によります。</span><span lang="en">External-authentication adapters verify method-specific signatures, issuer, audience, expiry, callback state, and related conditions. Verified external subjects map to internal UserAccounts through the provider and a stable subject identifier. This avoids incorrect linking based only on email addresses; external tokens are not used directly as internal sessions or Domain authority. Unverified credentials, disallowed methods, and unregistered adapters fail authentication. Availability of each method depends on implemented adapters and deployment configuration.</span>

<span lang="ja">認証方式ごとの検証を専用プロバイダーへ集約し、成功した結果を共通の認証状態へ揃えると、業務処理が方式ごとに資格情報を解釈する箇所を減らせます。Textus/CNCFは、人間の認証結果を内部のAccessSession・RefreshSessionへ統一し、共通の実行コンテキストへ引き継ぎます。方式固有の検証と業務上の認可を分離することで、異なる入口でも一貫した主体の扱いを保ちます。</span><span lang="en">Concentrating method-specific verification in dedicated providers and normalizing successful results into common authentication state reduces the places where business code must interpret credentials. Textus/CNCF normalizes human authentication results into internal AccessSession and RefreshSession state and carries them into the shared execution context. Separating method-specific verification from business authorization preserves consistent handling of subjects across entry points.</span>

### Internal Authentication State and AuthHandle Coordination｜内部の認証状態とAuthHandleによる連携

<span lang="ja">SecurityContextは、実行基盤が認証結果から構築する主体・認証状態の受渡し形式です。認可では、そこから認証状態、役割、スコープ、グループ、権限、業務境界の属性などを正規化したSecuritySubjectを利用します。各業務処理が外部claimを独自に読み直して権限を組み立てる方式にしません。</span><span lang="en">SecurityContext is the runtime carrier built from authentication results. Authorization uses SecuritySubject, which normalizes authentication state, roles, scopes, groups, capabilities, and business-boundary attributes. Business handlers do not independently reinterpret external claims to construct authority.</span>

<span lang="ja">Cloud Function連携では、中央のUser Managementが解決した認証状態への、有効期間を持つ不透明な参照としてAuthHandleを用います。AuthHandleはUserId、外部OAuthトークン、権限一覧、直列化したExecutionContextではありません。Applicationはその内容を編集して権限を増やさず、対象Domainへ参照を渡します。</span><span lang="en">Cloud Function coordination uses AuthHandle as an opaque, bounded-lifetime reference to authentication state resolved by central User Management. It is not a UserId, external OAuth token, capability list, or serialized ExecutionContext. Applications pass the reference to target Domains rather than editing it to increase authority.</span>

<span lang="ja">一つのApplication Operationが複数Domainを連携させる場合も、同じ有効なAuthHandleを利用できます。各Domainは参照を解決し、対象操作と資源について自分の方針で認可します。有効期限、アカウントやセッションの無効化、失効とキャッシュの扱いを合わせて定め、古い参照が無制限に権限を維持しないようにします。</span><span lang="en">An Application Operation coordinating several Domains may reuse the same valid AuthHandle. Each Domain resolves the reference and applies its own authorization policy to operations and resources. Expiry, account or session deactivation, revocation, and cache behavior must be defined together so that stale references do not preserve authority indefinitely.</span>

### Connect Domain API for Cloud Functions to the Common Authorization Path｜Cloud Function向けDomain APIで認証情報を共通の認可経路へ接続する

<span lang="ja">Cloud Function向けDomain APIは、Operation要求、AuthHandle、Cloud Functionまたはサービスの識別情報、必要な観測文脈を受け取ります。これらを信頼境界で解決し、Domainが利用するSecurityContextとExecutionContextへ正規化します。Applicationから渡された任意のclaimを、そのまま権限にはしません。</span><span lang="en">Domain API for Cloud Functions receives the Operation request, AuthHandle, calling Cloud Function or service identity, and required observation context. It resolves them at the trust boundary and normalizes them into Domain SecurityContext and ExecutionContext. Arbitrary Application-supplied claims do not become authority.</span>

<span lang="ja">正規化後は通常のOperation呼出しへ合流し、Operation認可を経てActionCallを実行します。その処理が発行するUnitOfWorkには対象資源の認可を適用します。Applicationの実行方式や、その外側のPresentation技術が異なっても、Domain内部では同じ判定経路を利用します。</span><span lang="en">After normalization, requests enter the ordinary Operation path, pass Operation authorization, and execute ActionCall. UnitOfWork requests issued by that processing receive target-resource authorization. The Domain uses the same decision path regardless of the Application execution form or the Presentation technology outside it.</span>

### Establish Authorization Foundations with SimpleEntity Metadata and Defaults｜SimpleEntityの基本情報と既定値で認可の基礎を揃える

<span lang="ja">認可機構があっても、所有者や権限の情報がデータごとに異なったり、作成時に設定されなかったりすると、対象単位の判定を一律に適用できません。個別開発では、この情報構造と保存・参照の扱いを揃える作業が、細かな認可を実装する際の制約になります。</span><span lang="en">Even with authorization mechanisms, inconsistent ownership or permission data, or missing initialization, prevents uniform object-level decisions. In bespoke development, aligning this information and its persistence and retrieval becomes a practical constraint on implementing fine-grained authorization.</span>

<span lang="ja">SimpleEntityは、UNIX型のowner・group・otherに基づく権限情報を共通の基本情報として持ちます。SecurityAttributesは所有者とグループの識別情報、および各区分のread・write・execute権を保持します。認証機構が確認した主体とその所属を、この対象側の情報へ対応付けてアクセスを判断します。ライフサイクル、公開、監査の基本情報も、状態や公開期間に関する条件と追跡を支えます。</span><span lang="en">SimpleEntity carries common permission metadata based on the UNIX-style owner/group/other model. SecurityAttributes holds owner and group identities and read/write/execute rights for each category. Access decisions relate the subject and memberships established through authentication to this target-side information. Lifecycle, publication, and audit metadata also support state and publication-window conditions and traceability.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準の開発経路では、Entity作成時に所有者情報と権限を補完します。利用者の権限で読み書きする経路では、owner・group・otherのread・write権を自動判定します。業務用Entityの既定値は次表のとおりで、公開コンテンツはpublic-readなどの明示的なプロファイルで扱います。サービス内部や基盤処理の実行モードは、後述のUnitOfWork認可で区別します。</span><span lang="en">Standard paths supply ownership and permissions when an Entity is created. Paths operating under user permissions automatically check owner/group/other read/write rights. The following table shows business-Entity defaults; public content uses explicit profiles such as public-read. Service-internal and framework execution modes are distinguished in the UnitOfWork authorization section.</span>

<span lang="ja">業務用Entityの既定権限</span><span lang="en">Default Permissions for Business Entities</span>

| <span lang="ja">区分</span><span lang="en">Category</span> | <span lang="ja">read</span><span lang="en">read</span> | <span lang="ja">write</span><span lang="en">write</span> | <span lang="ja">execute</span><span lang="en">execute</span> |
|---|---|---|---|
| <span lang="ja">owner（所有者）</span><span lang="en">owner</span> | <span lang="ja">許可</span><span lang="en">Allow</span> | <span lang="ja">許可</span><span lang="en">Allow</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> |
| <span lang="ja">group（グループ）</span><span lang="en">group</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> |
| <span lang="ja">other（その他）</span><span lang="en">other</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> | <span lang="ja">不許可</span><span lang="en">Deny</span> |

<span lang="ja">この共通情報と判定経路を使って、役割・関係・属性・状態に応じた認可を組み合わせます。各手法が権限の付与と条件の確認をどう分担するかを、次節で説明します。</span><span lang="en">The same metadata and decision paths support authorization based on roles, relationships, attributes, and state. The next section explains how these methods divide responsibility for grants and conditions.</span>

### The Authorization Decision Model｜誰が何をできるかを判断する認可モデル

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFは、役割、対象EntityのPermission、主体と対象の関係から有効な権限を求め、属性・状態・実行条件をGuardで確認します。これらをCapabilityとGuardの共通モデルで評価します。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF derives effective authority from roles, target-Entity Permission, and subject-target relationships, and checks attributes, state, and execution conditions through Guards. These are evaluated through a shared Capability-and-Guard model.</span>

<span lang="ja">Capabilityは許可された操作能力です。主体に与える権限に加え、対象EntityのPermissionや関係から、その対象に限った権限を求めます。すべてのEntityの権限を利用者側へ列挙する必要はありません。</span><span lang="en">A Capability is an allowed ability to perform an action. In addition to subject grants, target-specific authority is derived from Entity Permission or relationships; permissions for every Entity need not be enumerated on the user.</span>

<span lang="ja">Guardは、その権限を現在の対象と状況で使える条件を確認します。権限の付与源ではありません。判定には、Guardを満たすことと、有効なCapabilityが対象操作の要求を満たすことの両方が必要です。</span><span lang="en">A Guard checks conditions under which authority may be used for the current target and context; it does not grant authority. A decision requires both satisfied Guards and effective Capabilities meeting the requested action’s requirements.</span>

<span lang="ja">設計方針：運用上の特権は数値のレベルで管理し、代表値に root、admin、application admin、user などの名前を対応づけます。各レベルには基本Capabilityの集合があり、割り当てた対象範囲ごとに追加・除外できます。例えばアプリAの管理者に監査ログの閲覧を追加しても、アプリBには適用されません。追加と除外が重なる場合は除外を優先します。</span><span lang="en">Design policy: operational privileges use numeric levels with names such as root, admin, application admin and user. Each level supplies a baseline set of capabilities. Additions and exclusions apply within the assignment’s scope, with exclusions taking precedence. Granting audit-log access to an administrator for application A applies only within A.</span>

<span lang="ja">主体に割り当てるレベルと、Entityの操作に必要なレベルは別々に指定します。通常のEntityは user を既定とし、例えば非公開の資料を読むには、所有者や対象別の閲覧権も確認します。所有者の変更から特権レベルを導出しません。信頼できる管理経路で root を行使する主体は、管理専用Entityを含むすべてのEntityを参照・更新できます。同じ利用者でも、通常のアプリ経由では管理専用Entityを直接取得できず、一覧・検索・投影にも現れません。</span><span lang="en">Distinguish the level assigned to a subject from the level required to operate on an Entity. Ordinary Entities default to user; reading a private document still requires the applicable ownership or object-access checks. Changing the owner does not assign a privilege level. A subject exercising root through the trusted management route can read and update every Entity, including management-only records. Application routes exclude management-only records from direct reads, lists, search results and projections, including requests from that same user.</span>

<span lang="ja">実装方針：初期段階はレベル・操作・対象範囲の固定表で判定し、Capability評価へ移行するときは同じ許可・拒否例で結果を照合します。現行コードには所有者の値を特権の既定値に使う経路があり、この設計を適用するには保存済みデータの扱いも決める必要があります。具体的な数値とその順序は今後確定します。</span><span lang="en">Implementation plan: initially use a fixed table of levels, operations and scopes. When adopting capability evaluation, verify it against the same allow and deny cases. Existing code paths default the privilege field from the owner, so adoption includes deciding how to interpret persisted values. Numeric assignments and ordering remain to be specified.</span>

<span lang="ja">用途別の手法と設定対象を次の表に整理します。任意形式のACLは現在の標準Permissionとは区別する拡張項目です。ServiceInternalやSystemなどの実行モードも、利用者の対象別権限とは分け、明示された用途で使用します。</span><span lang="en">The following table relates application-specific methods to configuration inputs. Arbitrary ACL lists are an extension distinct from the current standard Permission model. Execution modes such as ServiceInternal and System are also distinct from user object-level permissions and are used for their explicitly declared purposes.</span>

<span lang="ja">用途に応じた認可手法と設定対象</span><span lang="en">Authorization methods and configuration inputs</span>

| <span lang="ja">手法・機構</span><span lang="en">Method/mechanism</span> | <span lang="ja">設定する情報</span><span lang="en">Configuration inputs</span> | <span lang="ja">適用する範囲</span><span lang="en">Application scope</span> |
|---|---|---|
| <span lang="ja">RBAC：役割に応じた認可</span><span lang="en">RBAC: role-based authorization</span> | <span lang="ja">利用者・サービスの役割とOperationの要求</span><span lang="en">User/service roles and Operation requirements</span> | <span lang="ja">担当者・管理者など、業務機能を利用できる範囲を指定する</span><span lang="en">Define which business functions staff, administrators, or other roles may use</span> |
| <span lang="ja">DAC／Permission：所有者・グループ単位</span><span lang="en">DAC/Permission: owner and group access</span> | <span lang="ja">SimpleEntityの所有者・グループ・その他のread/write/execute</span><span lang="en">SimpleEntity owner/group/other read/write/execute rights</span> | <span lang="ja">対象データごとに閲覧・更新等を許可する</span><span lang="en">Grant read, update, and other access per target object</span> |
| <span lang="ja">ReBAC：主体と対象の関係</span><span lang="en">ReBAC: subject-target relationships</span> | <span lang="ja">主体とEntityの属性対応、関係に許す操作</span><span lang="en">Subject/Entity attribute matches and actions granted by a relation</span> | <span lang="ja">注文した顧客に、その注文の閲覧を許可する</span><span lang="en">Allow a customer to read the order they placed</span> |
| <span lang="ja">ABAC／Guard：属性と状況による条件</span><span lang="en">ABAC/Guard: attribute and contextual conditions</span> | <span lang="ja">テナント、公開状態、公開期間などの条件</span><span lang="en">Conditions such as tenant, publication state, and publication window</span> | <span lang="ja">権限があっても条件外の対象を拒否し、一覧の可視範囲も絞る</span><span lang="en">Reject out-of-condition targets despite a grant and narrow list visibility</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Capability：具体的な操作能力</span><span lang="en">Capability: specific action authority</span> | <span lang="ja">操作、コレクション、関連、Storeなどへの要求権限</span><span lang="en">Required authority for operations, collections, associations, or stores</span> | <span lang="ja">特定コレクションへの作成や、指定した関連の変更を許可する</span><span lang="en">Permit creation in a selected collection or mutation of a specified association</span> |
| <span lang="ja">privilege・実行条件：管理機能等の制限</span><span lang="en">Privilege and execution conditions: administrative restrictions</span> | <span lang="ja">権限の上限、実行モード、匿名利用、機能の有効化</span><span lang="en">Privilege ceiling, execution mode, anonymous access, and feature enablement</span> | <span lang="ja">管理者という役割だけで許可せず、本番環境の管理操作を限定する</span><span lang="en">Constrain production administration beyond merely having an administrator role</span> |

### Refine Default Protection into Application-Specific Permission Scope｜既定の保護から用途別の許可範囲へ絞り込む

<span lang="ja">用途別の規則は、CMLのACCESS、Operationの認可メタデータ、資源別の設定へ記述します。Entityやコレクション単位の既定値を起点に、必要な公開範囲と操作を指定します。</span><span lang="en">Application-specific rules are declared through CML ACCESS, Operation authorization metadata, and resource-specific configuration. Entity or collection defaults provide the starting point for specifying required visibility and actions.</span>

<span lang="ja">許可範囲は、Component・Service・Operation、コレクションや対象Entity、read・update・deleteなどの操作、属性や状態の条件を組み合わせて指定します。作成はまだ対象Entityがないためコレクション単位で判断し、search/listは呼出し権限に加えて結果の可視範囲を絞ります。関連の変更やStoreの管理にも、それぞれの資源と操作に対応する規則を適用します。</span><span lang="en">Permission scope combines Component/Service/Operation, collection or target Entity, actions such as read/update/delete, and attribute or state conditions. Creation is authorized at collection level because the Entity does not yet exist; search/list additionally narrows result visibility. Association changes and Store administration use rules for their respective resources and actions.</span>

<span lang="ja">例えば、資料編集Operationを編集担当者に許可し、対象資料は担当関係を持つものに限定し、同一テナントかつ編集中というGuardを適用します。対象を担当資料だけに限定する場合は、所有者・グループ等の別の付与経路でも意図しない許可が生じないよう設定します。</span><span lang="en">For example, document-editing Operations can be available to editors, target documents limited to assigned ones, and Guards require the same tenant and an editable state. When access must be limited to assigned documents, other grant paths such as owner/group permissions are configured to avoid unintended grants.</span>

<span lang="ja">この精密な指定は、過大な権限を減らし、誤操作や侵害時に操作できる対象を限定します。SimpleEntityが判断材料を揃え、モデル・設定が用途を表し、共通のOperation・UnitOfWork判定が実行へ適用することで、基本的な保護から細かな認可まで同じ開発経路で扱えます。</span><span lang="en">Precise scope reduces excessive authority and limits the targets that mistakes or compromise can affect. SimpleEntity supplies decision inputs, models and configuration express application policy, and shared Operation and UnitOfWork checks enforce it. The same development path therefore supports both baseline protection and fine-grained authorization.</span>

### Authorize Operation Invocation Before Execution｜Operationを呼び出せるかを実行前に判定する

<span lang="ja">Operation認可は、Component・Service・Operationを呼び出せるかを判定します。Subsystemは認証状態を解決した後、ActionCallを作成・実行する前にこの判定を行います。Web、REST、コマンドなどの入口を共通の判定へ集め、Web側で許可されたことだけを理由に業務処理を開始しません。</span><span lang="en">Operation authorization decides whether a Component/Service/Operation may be invoked. After resolving authentication state, the Subsystem evaluates the rule before creating or executing ActionCall. Web, REST, command, and other ingress paths converge here; Web admission alone does not start business logic.</span>

<span lang="ja">ルールには匿名利用の可否、実行モード、必要なprivilege、役割、スコープ、Capabilityなどを記述します。Operation定義、CMLの生成メタデータ、Subsystemの宣言を共通のルールへ反映し、各ハンドラーが認可関数を呼び忘れないことに依存しません。</span><span lang="en">Rules describe anonymous access, execution modes, required privilege, roles, scopes, and Capabilities. Operation definitions, generated CML metadata, and Subsystem declarations feed a common runtime rule rather than relying on every handler to remember an authorization call.</span>

<span lang="ja">例えば「資料編集」のOperationを呼び出す権限があっても、他の組織が所有する資料を編集できるとは限りません。Operation認可は業務処理へ入るための判定であり、実際の対象Entityへのアクセスは次のUnitOfWork境界で改めて判定します。</span><span lang="en">Permission to invoke a document-editing Operation does not necessarily permit editing a document owned by another organization. Operation authorization admits business processing; access to the actual Entity is evaluated separately at the UnitOfWork boundary.</span>

### Authorize Target-Entity Access at UnitOfWork｜UnitOfWorkで対象Entityへのアクセスを判定する

<span lang="ja">業務処理が対象Entityを読み書きする際は、保護された内部DSLからUnitOfWorkを発行し、UnitOfWorkInterpreterで認可します。主体、対象コレクション・Entity、操作種別、関係、実行条件を合わせて評価します。Operationへ入れたことだけでは、任意のデータにアクセスできません。</span><span lang="en">Business processing issues UnitOfWork requests through the protected internal DSL, and UnitOfWorkInterpreter authorizes Entity access. The decision combines subject, collection and Entity, access kind, relations, and execution conditions. Admission to an Operation does not permit arbitrary data access.</span>

<span lang="ja">既存EntityではPermissionや関係をread・update・delete等の要求権限へ対応付けます。実行用の投影データに必要な権限情報がない場合は、永続化側の正規レコードを参照します。作成はコレクションや資源クラス単位で判定し、利用者の権限によるsearch/listでは結果の可視範囲も絞ります。</span><span lang="en">For existing Entities, Permission and relationships map to required authority for read, update, delete, and other actions. When an execution projection lacks required permission metadata, the canonical persisted record is consulted. Creation is authorized at collection or resource-class level; search/list under user permissions also restricts result visibility.</span>

<span lang="ja">利用者のPermissionを評価するUserPermission、サービス内部のServiceInternal、基盤処理のSystemを区別します。内部処理やSystemは明示された実行上の役割であり、ネットワークの内側にいるという理由で選ぶものではありません。Componentを越えるサービスアクセスには、明示的なサービス権限が必要になります。</span><span lang="en">Distinguish UserPermission, ServiceInternal, and System access modes. Internal and System processing are declared execution roles, not consequences of network location. Cross-Component service access requires an explicit service grant.</span>

<span lang="ja">Operation認可が呼出しの入口を制御し、UnitOfWork認可が処理中の対象資源を制御します。同じSecurityContextを基に判断し、拒否理由は共通の診断・観測へ渡します。業務コードからの直接的なStoreアクセスを通常経路にせず、さらにSandboxで利用可能な資源と消費量を制限します。</span><span lang="en">Operation authorization controls entry, while UnitOfWork authorization controls resources used during execution. Both use the same SecurityContext and report denials through common diagnostics and observation. Direct Store access from business code is not the normal path; Sandbox additionally limits available resources and consumption.</span>

### Carry Authorization into ExecutionContext and Sandbox｜認可結果をExecutionContextとSandboxへ引き継ぐ

<span lang="ja">認証された主体、認可に使う条件、資源の利用上限を共通の実行文脈で運ぶと、処理の途中でも同じ主体と制約を基に判定できます。OperationとUnitOfWorkは操作・対象への権限を確認し、Safety Sandboxはファイル、ネットワーク、プロセス、DataStoreなどの利用範囲と消費量を制限します。この分担を共通の文脈で接続することが、認可と資源制御の食い違いを減らします。</span><span lang="en">Carrying the authenticated subject, authorization conditions, and resource limits in a shared execution context enables checks throughout processing to use the same subject and constraints. Operation and UnitOfWork checks assess authority over operations and targets; Safety Sandbox limits access to and consumption of files, networks, processes, DataStores, and other resources. Connecting these responsibilities through common context reduces discrepancies between authorization and resource control.</span>

<span lang="ja">ExecutionContextはSecurityContext、Sandbox、資源上限、観測情報などの実行条件を保持します。実行基盤が構築・管理する文脈を業務処理へ渡し、各処理が個別のパラメータから権限情報を独自に組み立てる箇所を減らします。</span><span lang="en">ExecutionContext holds SecurityContext, Sandbox, resource limits, observation information, and other execution conditions. The runtime constructs and manages this context and passes it to business processing, reducing places where individual handlers independently reconstruct authority from separate parameters.</span>

### Constrain Admitted Execution Through Safety Sandbox｜許可された実行範囲をSafety Sandboxで制限する

<span lang="ja">Safety Sandboxは、悪意あるコードに加え、バグ、誤操作、AIの誤判断による許可範囲外の資源操作も制限対象とします。</span><span lang="en">Safety Sandbox limits unauthorized resource actions arising from malicious code, bugs, operational mistakes, and AI errors.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/sandbox-authority-limits-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/sandbox-authority-limits-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">業務上の認可、外部資源への権限、消費量の制限を分け、ExecutionContextを通して同じ実行へ適用します。</span><span lang="en">Business authorization, external-resource permissions, and consumption limits remain distinct and are connected to execution through ExecutionContext.</span>

<span lang="ja">ExecutionContext、SandboxContext、Capability、ExecutionLimitsを用いて、ファイル、ネットワーク、プロセス、HTTP、DataStore、外部サービスの利用権限と資源消費を制限します。</span><span lang="en">ExecutionContext, SandboxContext, Capability, and ExecutionLimits constrain authority and resource consumption for files, networks, processes, HTTP, DataStores, and external services.</span>

<span lang="ja">AIへの指示やSkillは行動を案内します。Sandboxは、実行基盤が認めていない操作を拒否することで、その案内を技術的な制限で補います。</span><span lang="en">Instructions and Skills guide AI behavior. Sandbox complements that guidance with technical restrictions by rejecting operations not admitted by the runtime.</span>

<span lang="ja">hard limitは実行主体が越えられない上限です。soft limitは、許可された実行文脈で上限の範囲内に調整します。何を利用できるかと、どれだけ消費できるかを分けて設定します。</span><span lang="en">Hard limits cannot be exceeded by the execution subject. Soft limits can be adjusted within those bounds by an authorized execution context. Authority to use a resource and the amount that may be consumed are configured separately.</span>

<span lang="ja">Sandboxは利用可能な権限と資源を制限するが、許可範囲内の処理が業務上正しいことまで判定するものではありません。入力モデルや標準API、業務規則の検査と組み合わせ、残る異常には観測・封じ込め・復旧で対処します。</span><span lang="en">Sandbox limits authority and resources; it does not establish that behavior within those limits is correct for the business. Combine it with input models, standard APIs, and business-rule checks, and address remaining anomalies through observation, containment, and recovery.</span>

### Reduce Authentication Load with Bounded Caches｜保持範囲を限定したキャッシュで認証基盤の負荷を抑える

<span lang="ja">認証状態への参照を再利用するキャッシュは、同じ要求に伴う繰返しの認証状態照会を減らし、User ManagementとUser DBの負荷を抑えます。保持する場所、容量、有効期間を限定することで、参照の複製範囲と保持量も管理できます。これは認証基盤の可用性と情報管理への寄与であり、操作の許可はAuthHandleの有効性と各Domainの認可によって判定します。</span><span lang="en">Reusing references to authentication state reduces repeated state lookups associated with requests and lowers load on User Management and the User DB. Bounding storage location, capacity, and lifetime also controls where references are replicated and how much is retained. This contributes to authentication-service availability and information management; permission to perform an operation is determined through AuthHandle validity and each Domain's authorization.</span>

<span lang="ja">Cloud Functionの標準キャッシュは、credentialのfingerprintまたは証拠の識別情報からAuthHandleへの、容量とTTLを制限したインスタンス内メモリーとします。AuthHandleは有効期間を持つ不透明な参照であり、キャッシュの永続化やインスタンス間共有は前提にしません。キャッシュのTTLとAuthHandle自体の有効期限、セッションの無効化・失効の扱いを合わせて検証します。</span><span lang="en">The standard Cloud Function cache is instance-local memory mapping credential fingerprints or evidence identifiers to AuthHandles, with bounded capacity and TTL. An AuthHandle is an opaque reference with a validity period; persistent or cross-instance shared caching is not assumed. Cache TTL, AuthHandle expiration, and session invalidation and revocation behavior are verified together.</span>

<span lang="ja">キャッシュに該当がなければUser Managementへ問い合わせます。User Managementも自分のメモリー・キャッシュを利用してからUser DBへアクセスします。通常経路はCloud Function内メモリー、User Management内メモリー・キャッシュ、User DBの順になります。</span><span lang="en">A cache miss calls User Management. User Management uses its own memory and caches before accessing the User DB. The normal path is Cloud Function instance memory, then User Management memory and caches, then the User DB.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準構成ではインスタンス内のキャッシュを利用し、保持先と通信経路を絞ります。Redisなどの外部共有キャッシュは、実測に基づく拡張性の要求がある場合に検討します。その際は、追加する通信、整合性管理、保持情報、運用上の保護を、負荷軽減の効果と合わせて評価します。</span><span lang="en">The standard configuration uses instance-local caches to keep storage locations and communication paths limited. External shared caches such as Redis are considered when measured scalability requirements justify them. Their additional communication, consistency management, retained information, and operational protection are evaluated alongside the expected load reduction.</span>

## Reduce Defects and Disclosure in Authorized Processing｜許可された処理の欠陥と情報漏洩を減らす

<span lang="ja">正しい利用者からの許可された要求でも、入力処理、出力、データ更新、機微情報の取扱いに欠陥があれば、情報漏洩や意図しない操作につながります。</span><span lang="en">Even an authorized request from the intended user can lead to disclosure or unintended actions if input handling, output, data updates, or sensitive-information handling is defective.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準APIと入力モデルに一般的な対策を組み込み、機微情報の分類で保持・出力の範囲を定めます。</span><span lang="en">Common controls are built into standard APIs and input models, while sensitive-information classifications define retention and output scope.</span>

<span lang="ja">これらは、許可された処理の中で起こる実装上の欠陥を減らす役割を担います。認可と資源制限による影響範囲の抑制と組み合わせます。</span><span lang="en">These controls reduce implementation defects within authorized processing and complement the impact limits imposed by authorization and resource restrictions.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準経路と例外経路の分担、および機微情報を保持・委譲する判断を以下で説明します。</span><span lang="en">The following sections explain the standard and exception paths and decisions about retaining or delegating sensitive information.</span>

### Safe-by-Construction Application Security｜構造によって安全性を確保するアプリケーション開発

<span lang="ja">入力モデルと型付きRepository/DataStore APIは、サーバー側で扱う入力とデータ操作を制約します。TextusがHTMLを生成する経路では、出力文脈に応じたレンダラーで出力を保護し、HTTPの更新操作には入口のCSRF方針を適用します。</span><span lang="en">Input models and typed Repository/DataStore APIs constrain server-side inputs and data operations. Where Textus generates HTML, a context-aware renderer protects that output, and HTTP mutations follow the ingress CSRF policy.</span>

<span lang="ja">SQL文字列の直接連結、信頼できない値のHTMLへの直接挿入、直接のファイル・ネットワーク・プロセス操作は、標準経路から外れる箇所として識別し、lintとレビューの対象にします。入力は宣言したOperation入力モデルへ束縛し、Entityへの無制限の一括代入や安全でないデシリアライズを避けます。</span><span lang="en">Direct SQL concatenation, inserting untrusted values directly into HTML, and direct file, network, or process access are identified as departures from standard paths and inspected by lint and review. Inputs are bound to declared Operation input models rather than unrestricted Entity assignment or unsafe deserialization.</span>

<span lang="ja">TypeScriptやFlutterなどで独立したPresentationを実装する場合、受け取ったデータを描画する際のエスケープや安全なAPIの選択は、そのUI基盤で適用します。Textus側はAPIへの入力、返却するデータの認可・範囲、機微情報を制御します。担当位置を分けることで、サーバーの標準APIによる保護とPresentation側の出力保護を接続します。</span><span lang="en">For an independent Presentation built with TypeScript, Flutter, or another platform, escaping and safe rendering API choices are applied on that UI platform. Textus controls API inputs, authorization and scope of returned data, and sensitive information. This division connects protection through server-side standard APIs with output protection in the Presentation.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準APIは一般的な欠陥を起こしにくい実装経路を提供し、例外経路の検査はその範囲を外れる箇所を扱います。さらにSandboxで利用できる外部資源を限定します。認可済みの処理にも実装上の欠陥はあり得るため、これらを併用します。</span><span lang="en">Standard APIs provide implementation paths less prone to common defects; escape-hatch inspection covers departures from those paths. Sandbox additionally limits accessible external resources. These controls work together because authorized processing can still contain implementation defects.</span>

### Sensitive Information｜機微情報の取扱い

<span lang="ja">機微情報モデルでは、通常のDomain値、機微な個人情報、機微な識別情報、Credential、Secret、保持対象から除外する高度に機微な値、外部の機微情報へのReference/Resultを区別します。高価値の秘密や対話をプロバイダーまたはOSへ委譲できる場合はUIも含めて委ね、業務に必要な参照・表明・結果だけをTextus側へ戻します。</span><span lang="en">The sensitive-information model distinguishes ordinary Domain values, Sensitive Personal Data, Sensitive Identity, Credentials, Secrets, highly sensitive values excluded from retention, and external Sensitive References/Results. When a provider or operating system can own high-value secrets or interactions, delegation includes the UI where possible; only the business references, assertions, and results needed by Textus are returned.</span>

<span lang="ja">分類は名称を付けるだけでなく、業務に保持する情報、外部へ委譲する処理、ログやトレースへ出してよい情報の判断に用います。保有する機微情報を減らすことと、権限・出力経路を限定することを組み合わせて、漏洩の機会と影響を抑えます。</span><span lang="en">Classification guides what business data is retained, which interactions are delegated, and what may enter logs and traces. Combining reduced retention with authority and output-path limits reduces opportunities for disclosure and its effects.</span>

<span lang="ja">外部identityはTextus内部のSubject/User IDへ対応付け、通常のDomainへ無制限に伝播させません。外部委譲は委譲先の安全性を本稿で保証するものではなく、返される参照・表明・結果と認可の接続を確認する必要があります。</span><span lang="en">Map external identities to internal Textus Subject/User IDs rather than propagating them without limits into ordinary Domains. Delegation is not a guarantee about the provider; returned references, assertions, and results must be checked in their authorization context.</span>

# Contain Incidents and Recover｜侵害や異常の影響を抑えて復旧する

<span lang="ja">予防策や権限制限があっても、許可された範囲の誤動作や実行環境の侵害は想定する必要があります。実行中の環境を安全と判断し続けることだけに運用を依存させません。</span><span lang="en">Prevention and authority limits still require planning for faulty behavior within admitted scope and for compromised execution environments. Operations must not depend solely on repeatedly declaring a running environment safe.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/operational-containment-recovery-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/operational-containment-recovery-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">実行環境の交換に加えて、権限の失効、永続状態の確認、原因の修正を組み合わせます。図は対応の関係を示し、一律の逐次実行を要求するものではありません。</span><span lang="en">Replacement is combined with revocation, persistent-state examination, and correction of causes. The diagram relates response activities rather than mandating one sequential schedule.</span>

<span lang="ja">共通経路で収集した監査・観測情報から、操作の経緯と異常の影響を確認します。対応では権限の失効、通信経路の隔離、実行環境の交換を選び、永続状態を確認して業務を復旧します。以下のHA・ローテーションは、この対応を支える配備・運用構成です。</span><span lang="en">Audit and observation records collected through shared paths support examination of operation history and incident impact. Responses select authority revocation, communication isolation, and runtime replacement, followed by persistent-state checks and business recovery. The HA and rotation arrangements below are deployment and operational configurations that support this response.</span>

<span lang="ja">Componentの契約と依存関係を、実行主体、認可結果、実行環境の観測情報へ対応付けます。区画ごとの権限制限で影響を絞り、共通の観測経路で全体を追うことで、失効・隔離・交換の対象を判断できます。</span><span lang="en">Component contracts and dependencies are associated with observations of execution subjects, authorization decisions, and execution environments. Compartment-specific authority limits constrain impact, while shared observability supports system-wide tracing and selection of revocation, isolation, and replacement targets.</span>

<span lang="ja">実行環境を交換しても、すでに生じた不正な業務更新や漏洩まで取り消せるわけではありません。観測情報と永続状態の確認、必要な業務上の復旧を別途行う前提で、この経路を運用します。</span><span lang="en">Replacing an execution environment does not undo unauthorized business updates or past disclosure. This recovery path assumes examination of observations and persistent state, with separate business recovery where needed.</span>

## Connect Security and Observability and Use Audit Trails｜セキュリティと可観測性を接続し、監査証跡を活用する

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFでは、セキュリティ制御と可観測性が共通の実行経路で連動します。Operation、認可、実行基盤、Subsystem、インフラストラクチャの情報を通常のOTLP経路へ集め、Control Center等から診断します。実行主体、Component、Operation、対象資源、判定結果を実行文脈やtraceId・correlationIdで対応付けることで、制御の結果と処理の経過を続けて確認できます。</span><span lang="en">In Textus/CNCF, security controls and observability cooperate along shared execution paths. Information from Operations, authorization, the runtime, Subsystems, and infrastructure is collected through the ordinary OTLP path for diagnosis through tools such as Control Center. Execution context and trace or correlation identifiers connect subjects, Components, Operations, target resources, and decisions, allowing control outcomes to be examined alongside processing behavior.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準のOperation実行とデータ更新の経路では、基盤が監査証跡（audit trail）を自動収集します。認可・永続化などの共通処理点で結果を記録し、SimpleEntityの作成者・作成日時・更新者・更新日時も基盤が設定・更新します。業務処理ごとに記録処理を個別実装する負担と記録漏れを減らし、誰が、いつ、どの対象へ、どの操作を行い、どの結果になったかを追う材料を揃えます。</span><span lang="en">Along standard Operation-execution and data-mutation paths, the platform automatically collects audit trails. Shared checkpoints such as authorization and persistence record outcomes, while the platform initializes and updates SimpleEntity creation and update identities and timestamps. This reduces per-handler recording code and omissions, supplying evidence of who performed which operation on what target, when, and with what outcome.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/security-observation-audit-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/security-observation-audit-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">実行文脈で記録を関連付け、診断と監査の目的に応じて利用します。Entityの更新メタデータと操作履歴は別の情報です。</span><span lang="en">Execution context correlates records for diagnosis and auditing. Entity update metadata and operation history are distinct information.</span>

<span lang="ja">可観測性は処理の経過や異常を診断し、監査はEventなどの一次的な事実を基に操作履歴と権限行使を確認します。両者は識別情報で関連付けますが、保存期間と閲覧権限はそれぞれの用途に合わせて設定します。Entityの作成・更新メタデータは追跡の手掛かりとして、操作履歴を表すEventや監査記録と併用します。</span><span lang="en">Observability diagnoses behavior and anomalies; auditing examines operation history and authority use using primary facts such as Events. Identifiers connect the two, while retention and read permissions follow each purpose. Entity creation/update metadata provides attribution cues and is used alongside Events and audit records that represent operation history.</span>

<span lang="ja">記録と利用目的の対応</span><span lang="en">Records and Their Uses</span>

| <span lang="ja">情報</span><span lang="en">Information</span> | <span lang="ja">役割</span><span lang="en">Role</span> | <span lang="ja">利用方法</span><span lang="en">Use</span> |
|---|---|---|
| <span lang="ja">ログ・トレース・メトリクス</span><span lang="en">Logs, traces, metrics</span> | <span lang="ja">経過・性能・異常の診断</span><span lang="en">Diagnose behavior, performance, anomalies</span> | <span lang="ja">処理の関連付け、異常検出、影響調査</span><span lang="en">Correlate processing, detect anomalies, investigate impact</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Event・監査記録</span><span lang="en">Events and audit records</span> | <span lang="ja">操作・結果・権限行使の事実</span><span lang="en">Facts about operations, outcomes, authority use</span> | <span lang="ja">操作履歴の確認、監査、事後調査</span><span lang="en">Review operation history, audit, investigate</span> |
| <span lang="ja">Entityの作成・更新メタデータ</span><span lang="en">Entity creation/update metadata</span> | <span lang="ja">対象データの作成・更新の帰属</span><span lang="en">Attribute creation and latest update</span> | <span lang="ja">履歴の記録と併用して対象を追跡</span><span lang="en">Trace targets together with history records</span> |

<span lang="ja">監査記録と診断情報をComponentの権限・依存関係・配備構成へ対応付けることで、部品をまたぐ影響範囲を調べ、失効・隔離・交換の対象を判断できます。記録を残す機構と、記録を使う監査・インシデント対応を接続します。</span><span lang="en">Relating audit records and diagnostics to Component authority, dependencies, and deployment configuration supports cross-component impact investigation and selection of revocation, isolation, and replacement targets. This connects recording mechanisms to audits and incident response.</span>

<span lang="ja">観測対象には判断に必要な識別情報と結果を残し、credential、token、不要な個人情報はログやトレースへ複製しません。診断に必要な情報を確保しながら、観測基盤自体に蓄積する機微情報と、その漏洩の影響を抑えます。</span><span lang="en">Observation retains identifiers and outcomes needed for decisions without copying credentials, tokens, or unnecessary personal data into logs and traces. This preserves diagnostic value while limiting sensitive information accumulated in the observation infrastructure and the impact of its disclosure.</span>

## Support Replacement with Immutable Artifacts and Prepared Environments｜不変の配布物と準備済み環境で交換を支える

<span lang="ja">受入れ済みの不変のCARと配備構成から実行環境を再構築できると、問題のある環境を隔離し、既知の構成へ交換できます。交換対象は配備単位で決まり、そこに含まれるComponentと依存先を確認します。</span><span lang="en">Reconstructing execution environments from admitted immutable CARs and deployment configuration allows a problematic environment to be isolated and replaced with a known configuration. The deployment unit determines replacement scope, including its components and dependencies.</span>

<span lang="ja">Domainティアは、Primaryが新規更新を受け付け、Read Replicaが許可された参照を提供する構成を取ります。StandbyはPrimaryへの昇格準備が整った性質であり、参照提供とは分けて確認します。準備済みの交換先を持つことで、メモリ常駐による応答性と環境の交換可能性を両立させる設計です。</span><span lang="en">The Domain uses a Primary for new mutations and Read Replicas for authorized reads. Standby describes readiness for promotion, which is checked separately from read service. Prepared replacements are designed to combine memory-resident responsiveness with replaceable environments.</span>

<span lang="ja">メモリ常駐の性能を活かしながら交換可能性を確保するため、待機系の準備と交代を組み合わせます。具体的な昇格・ドレインの手順は次節で説明します。</span><span lang="en">Preparing standby environments and rotating them preserves replacement capability while retaining the performance of memory-resident execution. The next section explains promotion and drain.</span>

<span lang="ja">モデルとティア分割で機能・権限・到達経路を限定し、不変の成果物から実行環境を再構築できるようにします。環境交換は、問題のある実行環境を隔離して既知の構成へ戻す手段です。</span><span lang="en">Models and tier separation limit functionality, authority, and reachable paths, while immutable artifacts allow runtime reconstruction. Replacement isolates a problematic runtime and returns execution to a known configuration.</span>

<span lang="ja">実行環境の変更方法と寿命は別の設計軸です。Mutableは稼働中の環境を更新し、Immutableは変更せず置換します。Ephemeralは寿命を短く管理する性質で、Immutableと組み合わせられます。Cloud Functionの短命性も、実行基盤の再利用・廃棄方針に応じて扱います。</span><span lang="en">How an environment changes and how long it lives are separate design axes. Mutable environments are updated in place; immutable environments are replaced. Ephemeral describes a short managed lifetime and can be combined with immutability. Cloud Function lifetimes also depend on runtime reuse and disposal policy.</span>

<span lang="ja">CNCFはメモリを高速化に使い、業務の継続に必要な状態を特定プロセスのメモリだけに残さない構造を意図しています。更新はDomainの規則とUnitOfWorkを通して正本へ確定し、キャッシュやViewはその結果から再構築できるようにします。実行環境の交換で確定データを失わないことは、保存先の永続化契約と回復手順を含めて確認します。途中の計算や結果不明の処理は、確定済みデータと区別します。</span><span lang="en">CNCF deliberately uses memory for acceleration without leaving continuity-critical state solely in one process. Domain rules and UnitOfWork govern authoritative commits, from which caches and Views can be reconstructed. Preserving committed data across replacement must be qualified with the storage durability contract and recovery procedure. Intermediate computation and uncertain outcomes remain distinct from committed data.</span>

<span lang="ja">環境の交換は、侵害状態が同じ実行環境に残る期間を抑えるために用います。資格情報の更新・失効、原因となった実装の修正、永続状態の確認との分担は「交換と業務上の復旧」で説明します。</span><span lang="en">Environment replacement limits how long a compromise persists in the same environment. Its relationship to credential renewal and revocation, correction of the implementation cause, and persistent-state checks is covered under replacement and business recovery.</span>

<span lang="ja">Applicationでは環境の再利用と廃棄、Domainではメモリ常駐性能を維持する準備済み環境への交代を選びます。更新・定期交換・セキュリティ対応は共通の交換機構を使い、障害時には別の権限・回復条件を適用します。採用理由、日常運用、費用と効果は[[../../immutable-infrastructure/textus-cncf-immutable-infrastructure.dox/index.dox][イミュータブルインフラストラクチャ技術ガイド]]、同期と切替えの詳細は[[../../availability/textus-cncf-availability-architecture.dox/index.dox][可用性・HA技術ガイド]]を参照します。</span><span lang="en">Application runtimes use reuse/disposal; the Domain rotates into prepared environments while retaining resident-memory performance. Updates, regular replacement and security response share a replacement mechanism, with distinct authority/recovery conditions for failure. See the [[../../immutable-infrastructure/textus-cncf-immutable-infrastructure.dox/index.dox][Immutable Infrastructure guide]] for adoption, operation and cost/effect, and [[../../availability/textus-cncf-availability-architecture.dox/index.dox][Availability and HA guide]] for synchronization and transfer details.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/tier-performance-security-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/tier-performance-security-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">ApplicationティアとDomainティアにおける性能とセキュリティの両立</span><span lang="en">Balancing performance and security in Application and Domain tiers</span>

<span lang="ja">図はApplicationの再利用・廃棄とDomainの準備・交代を概略で示します。図中のActiveは本文のPrimaryに対応し、Standbyは昇格準備を表します。Read Replicaとしての参照提供と、旧系の保持・退役条件は本文の説明に従います。時間幅は実際の所要時間を表しません。</span><span lang="en">The figure sketches Application reuse/disposal and Domain preparation/rotation. Its Active corresponds to Primary in the text; Standby denotes promotion readiness. Read Replica service and old-runtime retention/retirement follow the text conditions. Widths are not elapsed time.</span>

## Distinguish Planned Replacement from Failure and Compromise Response｜計画交換と障害・侵害への対応を分けて運用する

<span lang="ja">計画交換では、準備のできたBへ新しい参照・更新の受付を移し、旧Primary Aは受付済みの更新とその完了に必要な処理だけを継続します。交換用Read Replica Cを起動し、Aの遅い確定もB・Cへ同期します。Aは旧処理の結果が確定し、Cの準備、保持・観測と切戻しの条件を満たすまで、必要な同期を続けます。</span><span lang="en">During planned replacement, new read/update admission moves to ready B while former Primary A continues only admitted updates and required completion work. Start replacement Read Replica C and propagate late A commits to B/C. Keep A synchronized until old outcomes settle and replacement capacity, retention/observation and switch-back conditions are satisfied.</span>

<span lang="ja">旧Primaryは、予定時刻や保持時間だけを理由に廃棄しません。定期交換は起動・準備・切替え・排出を日常運用で確かめる方法であり、日次は固定の標準値ではありません。障害切替えでは旧権限の更新を実際の保存・実行境界で拒否し、新しい権限と準備を確認します。侵害が疑われる旧環境には、計画交換の切戻し方針を適用しません。</span><span lang="en">Do not discard a former Primary solely on a scheduled time or elapsed retention. Regular replacement exercises startup, readiness, transfer and drain; daily cadence is not a fixed default. Failover rejects invalid-authority effects at actual storage/execution boundaries and requires valid takeover authority and readiness. Planned fallback policy does not permit returning to a suspected compromised environment.</span>

<span lang="ja">この構成は、交換を特別な事故対応だけにせず、通常運用でも使えるようにする設計です。定期交換は侵害検出、永続データの正しさの確認、バックアップを代替しません。2026年11月13日時点ではPhase 108の先行実装項目は未着手で、ここで述べる更新保全・同期・交換の一体運用を実装済みとは扱いません。</span><span lang="en">This design makes replacement an ordinary operational path rather than an incident-only action. Regular replacement does not replace compromise detection, persistent-state checks or backups. As of 2026-11-13, Phase 108 first-delivery items remain open; integrated update preservation, synchronization and replacement are not claimed implemented.</span>

## Combine Replacement with Business Recovery｜交換と業務上の復旧を組み合わせる

<span lang="ja">優先する流れは、権限を限定し、観測・検出し、影響を封じ込めて権限を失効させ、不変の実行環境へ交換し、権威ある永続状態から復旧することです。一方、配布時の脅威モデルに必要な成果物の完全性検証まで不要とするものではありません。</span><span lang="en">The preferred flow limits authority, observes and detects, contains impact and revokes authority, replaces the immutable runtime, and recovers from authoritative persistent state. This does not remove the need for artifact-integrity verification where the distribution threat model requires it.</span>

<span lang="ja">脅威の要件で必要性を説明できない独自ハッシュ検査や大規模なロールバック機構は、複雑さや欠陥を増やすことがあります。実行環境の交換を基本経路とし、追加の完全性検査は対象とする脅威を明確にして選びます。</span><span lang="en">Custom hash checking or large rollback mechanisms without a justified threat requirement can add complexity and defects. Use environment replacement as the normal recovery path and select additional integrity checks for explicit threats.</span>

<span lang="ja">交換は問題のある実行環境を使い続けないための手段であり、漏洩した情報や不正な永続更新を取り消す手段ではありません。必要な状態確認と業務上の復旧を含めて、事故対応の範囲を定めます。</span><span lang="en">Replacement avoids continuing to use a problematic environment; it does not undo disclosure or unauthorized persistent changes. Define incident response to include necessary state examination and business recovery.</span>

## Security Lifecycle｜セキュリティのライフサイクル

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFのSecurity Harnessは概念的に次のlifecycleを構成します。</span><span lang="en">The Textus/CNCF Security Harness conceptually forms the following lifecycle.</span>

- <span lang="ja">予防：入力モデルと標準APIで、危険な操作を個別に実装する範囲を減らします。</span><span lang="en">Prevent: input models and standard APIs reduce the need to implement hazardous operations individually.</span>
- <span lang="ja">制約：CBDで限定した接点に共通の認可とSandboxを適用し、部品ごとの許可範囲を維持します。</span><span lang="en">Constrain: shared authorization and Sandbox controls enforce component-specific limits at interfaces bounded by CBD.</span>
- <span lang="ja">検証：モデルとCARの対応を検査し、検査した内容を配布先の受入れへ引き継ぎます。</span><span lang="en">Verify: inspect model-to-CAR correspondence and carry the inspected content into admission at the destination.</span>
- <span lang="ja">観測：主体・操作・対象・判定結果を共通の経路で追い、部品間の連携を含めて影響を調べます。</span><span lang="en">Observe: trace subjects, operations, targets, and decisions through common paths to assess impact across collaborating components.</span>
- <span lang="ja">封じ込め：権限と依存関係を基に失効・隔離の対象を定め、影響の拡大を抑えます。</span><span lang="en">Contain: use authority and dependency information to select revocation and isolation targets and limit propagation.</span>
- <span lang="ja">復旧：検証した配布物から環境を交換し、永続状態の確認と業務上の復旧を組み合わせます。</span><span lang="en">Recover: replace environments from verified artifacts and combine this with persistent-state checks and business recovery.</span>

<span lang="ja">予防と検証は欠陥の持込みを減らし、制約は持ち込まれた欠陥や侵害の作用を限定します。観測は残る異常を捉え、封じ込めと復旧を支えます。設計・配布・実行・運用の各段階へこれらを配置します。</span><span lang="en">Prevention and verification reduce defect introduction; constraints limit the effects of defects and compromise that remain. Observation identifies residual anomalies and supports containment and recovery. Place these roles across design, distribution, execution, and operations.</span>

# Use the Standard Configuration and Strengthen It for the Application｜標準構成を利用し、用途に合わせて強化する

<span lang="ja">導入では、標準経路で基本的な保護を利用し、業務固有の認可を設定します。公開範囲や情報の機微性に応じて、機能制限、区画分離、監査・復旧の構成を選びます。</span><span lang="en">Adoption starts with baseline protection through standard paths and business-specific authorization settings. Exposure and information sensitivity guide capability restrictions, compartment isolation, auditing, and recovery configurations.</span>

<span lang="ja">以下では、利用する提供物の確認、業務固有の設定、今後整備する運用パターンの順に整理します。既存機構の利用と、選択・設定を容易にする整備方針を分けて示します。</span><span lang="en">The following sections cover available components, business-specific settings, and planned operation patterns. They distinguish using existing mechanisms from plans to simplify selection and configuration.</span>

## Relating the Architecture to Available Capabilities｜設計の全体像と利用できる範囲を対応付ける

<span lang="ja">本書の技術一覧は、SimpleModelingとTextusがフルセットとして揃える設計上の範囲を示します。実際に利用できる範囲は、採用するTextus/CNCFの版、SAR/CAR、認証プロバイダー、配備構成によって定まります。例えば、共通の認証経路があっても、外部認証方式ごとの利用可否は提供済みアダプターと設定によります。</span><span lang="en">The technology inventory describes the architectural scope that SimpleModeling and Textus aim to provide as a full set. Available capabilities depend on the selected Textus/CNCF release, SARs and CARs, authentication providers, and deployment. For example, a shared authentication path does not determine which external authentication methods have available adapters and configuration.</span>

<span lang="ja">導入時には、各機構について、利用する提供物と版、必要な設定、動作を確認した範囲を対応付けます。開発中・未対応の項目は同じ保護範囲の中で識別し、拡充対象を明確にします。本書は設計の根拠と相互関係を扱い、提供状況の確定情報は各コンポーネントの仕様・リリース情報と照合します。</span><span lang="en">Adoption relates each mechanism to its supplying artifact and version, required configuration, and verified behavior. In-development and unsupported items are identified within the same coverage model so that expansion remains explicit. This guide explains design rationale and relationships; confirmed availability is checked against component specifications and release information.</span>

## Application-Specific Rules and the Scope of Standard Paths｜業務固有の規則と標準経路の適用範囲

<span lang="ja">基盤が提供するのは、認証・認可・制約・観測等を一貫して適用する機構です。どの利用者にどの業務操作を許可するか、どの情報を機微情報として扱うか、どの外部サービスを信頼するかは、業務の責任者と開発・運用担当者が定めます。SimpleModelingの作法は、それらの判断をモデルと設定へ置く場所を与えます。</span><span lang="en">The platform supplies consistent mechanisms for authentication, authorization, constraints, and observation. Business owners and development and operations teams determine permitted business actions, sensitive information, and trusted external services. SimpleModeling conventions provide explicit places for those decisions in models and configuration.</span>

<span lang="ja">標準APIを外れて直接SQL、ネットワーク、ファイル、プロセスを扱う経路は、通常の保護がどこまで適用されるかを確認する対象になります。例外経路を識別し、必要な権限と検査を明示することで、拡張を含むSAR/CARでも共通基盤との接続を保ちます。</span><span lang="en">Paths using direct SQL, network, filesystem, or process access outside standard APIs require an explicit assessment of which protections still apply. Identifying escape paths and their authority and checks maintains the connection to shared infrastructure when SARs and CARs are extended.</span>

## Move from Usable Defaults to Application-Specific Security Operation Patterns｜扱いやすいデフォルトから用途別の運用パターンへ進む

<span lang="ja">標準の扱いやすさを維持したまま、用途に必要な防御を少ない設定で選べるようにすることが、今後の整備方針です。個々の機構を組み合わせる知識を、再利用できる運用パターン・プロファイル・手順書としてまとめます。</span><span lang="en">The planned direction is to make application-appropriate protection selectable with a small number of settings while retaining standard usability. Knowledge about combining individual mechanisms will be packaged into reusable operation patterns, profiles, and guides.</span>

<span lang="ja">候補には、標準的な業務利用、外部公開、機微情報の取扱い、強い区画分離を必要とする用途があります。各パターンに、保護対象、対策の組合せ、効果、運用負担を示し、用途と負担から選べる構成にします。</span><span lang="en">Candidates include ordinary business use, public-facing services, sensitive information, and strong compartment isolation. Each pattern will describe protected assets, combined controls, effects, and operational burden so selection reflects application needs and cost.</span>

<span lang="ja">プロファイルは、選んだパターンに必要な設定をまとめて適用する役割を持ちます。既存の構想にあるCapability Profileで利用可能な機能を限定し、Security Profileで防御方針を選び、業務固有の認可をCMLと設定で指定する分担につなげます。用途別の組合せをあらかじめ整理することで、個々の機構を独立に設定する際の食い違いや適用漏れを減らします。</span><span lang="en">Profiles are intended to apply the settings required by a selected pattern as a coherent set. This builds on the existing design: Capability Profile limits available capabilities, Security Profile selects the protection posture, and CML and configuration specify business-specific authorization. Predefined combinations reduce inconsistent settings and omissions that can arise when mechanisms are configured independently.</span>

<span lang="ja">手順書では、パターンの選択から業務権限・配備の設定、許可・拒否と監査記録の確認、失効・復旧までを案内します。選んだ構成と実際の動作を対応付けることで、設定の簡略化と確認可能性を両立させます。</span><span lang="en">Guides will cover pattern selection, business-permission and deployment settings, allow/deny and audit-record checks, and revocation and recovery. Connecting the selected configuration to actual behavior combines simpler setup with verifiability.</span>

<span lang="ja">今後整備するパターン・プロファイル・手順書の分担</span><span lang="en">Planned Patterns, Profiles, and Guides</span>

| <span lang="ja">提供物</span><span lang="en">Planned provision</span> | <span lang="ja">定める内容</span><span lang="en">Defines</span> | <span lang="ja">組合せによる効果</span><span lang="en">Combined effect</span> |
|---|---|---|
| <span lang="ja">運用パターン</span><span lang="en">Operation pattern</span> | <span lang="ja">用途・保護対象・構成・効果・負担</span><span lang="en">Use, assets, configuration, effect, burden</span> | <span lang="ja">選ぶ構成の目的を明確にする</span><span lang="en">Clarifies why to select a configuration</span> |
| <span lang="ja">プロファイル</span><span lang="en">Profile</span> | <span lang="ja">機能制限・防御方針等の設定の組合せ</span><span lang="en">Settings for capability limits and protection posture</span> | <span lang="ja">少ない選択で整合した設定を適用する</span><span lang="en">Applies coherent settings through few choices</span> |
| <span lang="ja">設計・運用手順書</span><span lang="en">Design/operation guide</span> | <span lang="ja">業務設定・配備・確認・監査・復旧</span><span lang="en">Business settings, deployment, checks, auditing, recovery</span> | <span lang="ja">選択した構成を実際の運用につなげる</span><span lang="en">Connects the selected configuration to operation</span> |

## Conclusion｜まとめ

<span lang="ja">CMLとCBDが対象・操作・接点を定め、共通基盤が認証した主体に対して認可を適用します。標準経路ではEntityのUNIX型権限と既定値で基本的な保護を得られ、用途別の認可も同じ情報と判定機構に組み合わせられます。</span><span lang="en">CML and CBD define targets, operations, and interfaces, and shared infrastructure authorizes authenticated subjects. Standard paths provide baseline protection through UNIX-style Entity permissions and defaults, with application-specific authorization using the same information and decision mechanisms.</span>

<span lang="ja">ティアごとの信頼境界、資源制御、検査・配布の仕組みを組み合わせ、自動収集する記録を監査・観測・復旧へつなぎます。初学者にも扱いやすい標準運用を起点に、用途に応じた強化を選びやすくするパターン・プロファイル・手順書の整備を進める方針です。</span><span lang="en">Tier trust boundaries, resource controls, and inspection and distribution mechanisms work together, while automatically collected records support auditing, observation, and recovery. The planned patterns, profiles, and guides build on beginner-friendly standard operation to make application-specific hardening easier to select.</span>
